const n=JSON.parse(`{"intro":{"title":"Scenario IV: All Points West","check":"<ul><li>If the investigators played *Curse of the Rougarou* immediately before this scenario, read _Back on Track_. Otherwise, read _Right on Schedule_.</li></ul>","backOnTrack":"<p>_Back on Track:_ Your decision to pursue the rougarou put you a little far afield, but you return to New Orleans Union Station after a long and harrowing night to find the Dykstras' train waiting for you.</p>","whatAHorribleNight":"<p class='basic'>If an investigator has Curse of the Rougarou in their deck, read _What a Horrible Night_.</p><p>_What a Horrible Night_: Even when you have the urges controlled, there seem to be outward signs of the curse affecting you, given the looks from Ralph and Carrie. “I've got a razor and shaving cream in the caboose if you need it,” Ralph states, though you're not sure how seriously.</p><p class='basic'>Curse of the Rougarou gains “{'{'}reaction{'}'} After you release a {'{'}moon{'}'} token: Discard Curse of the Rougarou.”</p>","goodJuju":"<p class='basic'>If an investigator has Lady Esprit in their deck, read _Good Juju_.</p><p>_Good Juju_: Lady Esprit accompanies you to the station and wastes little time in setting up shop in the caboose. Carrie watches her with folded arms. “Are you a witch?” the young lady asks. Lady Esprit laughs with surprising spirit and continues without looking. “Even better than that, child.”</p><p class='basic'>Lady Esprit gains “{'{'}reaction{'}'} After you release a {'{'}moon{'}'} token: Discover a clue. (Limit once per round.)”</p>","fromNewOrleans":"Remember that \\"you're setting out from New Orleans.\\"","fromArkham":"Remember that \\"you're setting out from Arkham.\\"","rightOnSchedule":"<p>_Right on Schedule_: With time of the essence, you tell the Dykstras that you'll meet them at the Northside station and rapidly pack, also calling in a couple small favors to get some extra clothes for Thea to use during the journey. She keeps a close hold on the tome as you depart your house. “California. That'll give me time to read through this book, at least. Hopefully there's something in there that tells us what Blake is trying to do, or what my visions mean.”</p>","skipToSetup":"Skip to Setup","proceedToSetup":"Proceed to Setup"},"setup":{"gatherSets":"Gather all cards from the *All Points West*, *Cult of Shub-Niggurath*, *New Moon Daredevils*, and *Primordial Evils* encounter sets. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/all-points-west.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/cult-of-shub-niggurath.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/new-moon-daredevils.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/primordial-evils.png' /></section>","fromArkham":"If \\"you're setting out from Arkham,\\" during this scenario, use \\"Act 1 - Through the Forests (v.l).\\" Remove the other act 1 from the game.","fromNewOrleans":"If \\"you're setting out from New Orleans,\\" during this scenario, use \\"Act 1 - Through the Forests (v.II).\\" Remove the other act 1 from the game.","placeLocations":"Put the Locomotive Engine and Caboose locations into play. Randomly pick one of the _Freight Car_ and _Special Car_ locations and put them into play. Set each other copy of these locations aside, out of play. Each investigator begins play at Caboose. (*Each location begins play revealed.*)","allies":"Put Ralph Dykstra into play at Locomotive Engine. Put Carrie Dykstra into play at Caboose.","setAside":"Set the following cards aside, out of play: Each _Dark Young_ enemy, each _Circus Train_ location.","addTokens":"Based on the difficulty level, add the following chaos token(s) to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.","easy":"_Easy_: -2","standard":"_Standard_: -3","hard":"_Hard_: -4","expert":"_Expert_: -5"},"interludes":{"title":"Scenario Interlude: Now Arriving","notInThisTown":{"body":"<p>_Not in This Town:_ Your arrival in Chicago is timely, and you have the opportunity to interfere with the circus greatly before you both move onward. The Chicago police are constantly on edge with the gang activity common to the city, and with a little creative reporting to avoid sounding like a looney, you might convince them to go after Blake, though if it goes badly, the police might waylay you instead.</i></p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"We'll try to convince the cops to raid the circus.\\" Choose an investigator to test {'{'}intellect{'}'} or {'{'}agility{'}'}(3). This test gets + 1 {'{'}perPlayer{'}'} difficulty. Reduce the difficulty of this test by 1 for each _Police_, _Civic_, _Agency_ and _Veteran_ investigator chosen for this campaign. Investigators at any location may commit to this test. If you fail, place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>\\"We'll meddle on our own terms, however smaller.\\" Place 1 resource on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"raid":"“We'll try to convince the cops to raid the circus.”","smaller":"“We'll meddle on our own terms, however smaller.”"}},"wrongTerritory":{"body":"<p>_Wrong Territory:_ Your delays in getting to Chicago have limited your options in hampering the circus before you both must move on. The various crime families of the city compete with each other bitterly, and if you could somehow convince one of the dons that the circus is a front for bootlegging on their territory, it could set Blake back quite a bit, though if it goes badly, the gangs are likely to cause you plenty of trouble instead.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"We'll see if we can rile up the Chicago gangs.\\" Choose an investigator to test {intellect} or {agility} (4). This test gets +1 {perPlayer} difficulty. Reduce the difficulty of this test by 1 for each _Criminal_, _Socialite_, and _Entrepreneur_ investigator chosen for this campaign. Investigators at any location may commit to this test. If you fail, place 3 resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>\\"We'll meddle on our own terms, however smaller.\\" Place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"rileUp":"“We'll see if we can rile up the Chicago gangs.”","smaller":"“We'll meddle on our own terms, however smaller.”"}},"stompingGround":{"body":"<p>_Stomping Ground:_ Your timely arrival in Memphis gives you a chance to seek out former members of the New Moon Circus — or rather the Four Leaf Circus, as it used to be. You are able to locate Mr. Konkin, a former strongman who quit after witnessing some of the horrors in the making. He is reluctant to speak until you prove yourself capable of standing against Blake and his monstrous circus, though you will likely be set back by the time spent if you cannot.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"You want proof? Well you're gonna get it.\\" Choose an investigator to test {willpower} or {combat} (3). This test gets + 1 {perPlayer} difficulty. Reduce the difficulty of this test by 1 for each _Performer_, _Warden_, _Blessed_, and _Cursed_ investigator chosen for this campaign. Investigators at any location may commit to this test. If you fail, place 2 resources on the scenario reference card</li><li>\\"Getting back on track right away is more important.\\" Place 1 resource on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"proof":"“You want proof? Well you're gonna get it.”","backOnTrack":"“Getting back on track right away is more important.”"}},"foolsErrand":{"body":"<p>_Fool's Errand:_ With little time to spare before you move on, you decide to take a riskier approach to find answers. Locals direct you to an ancient forest outside of Memphis that was once home to grisly things that sound familiar to you now. It's possible that something yet remains that can give you insight into stopping Blake, but it's a matter of a needle in a haystack. You'll need to be persistent — and lucky — to find anything without misspending days here.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"Any advantage is worth braving a little danger.\\" Choose an investigator to test {willpower} or {combat} (4). This test gets +1 {perPlayer} difficulty. Reduce the difficulty of this test by 1 for each _Hunter_, _Believer_ and _Chosen_ investigator chosen for this campaign. Investigators at any location may commit to this test. If you fail, place 3 resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>\\"Getting back on track right away is more important.\\" Place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"braveDanger":"“Any advantage is worth braving a little danger.”","backOnTrack":"“Getting back on track right away is more important.”"}},"natureOfTheBeast":{"body":"<p>_Nature of the Beast:_ Upon your arrival in St. Louis, you inquire about the circus and find that there has been an “accident” involving them. Several laborers took the initiative to help unload the circus trains and were injured by the animals. While the official word is quick to attribute the attack to temperamental creatures, it's possible that the workers were attacked to prevent them from seeing anything. If you can help with their medical treatment, then you may get the laborers well enough to warn everyone about the circus. It's always easier to trust locals.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"Here, we can help patch them up.\\" Investigators as a group must discard cards from their hands and/or play areas with a total of 4 {perPlayer} or more skill icons. Reduce this amount by 2 for each _Medic_, _Assistant_, _Wayfarer_, and _Drifter_ investigator chosen for this campaign.</li><li>\\"We don't have the time or resources to help.\\" Place 1 resource on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"patchThemUp":"“Here, we can help patch them up.”","noTime":"“We don't have the time or resources to help.”"}},"skeletonsInTheCloset":{"body":"<p>_Skeletons in the Closet:_ You arrive in St. Louis with only a few hours to spare. You need to find something to hamper the circus activities quickly, something that the authorities can't overlook. It occurs to you that the monsters need tremendous amounts of food over the journey, and if you can dig up some evidence of extra meat in their diet, then you may save some other lives tonight.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"You just have to know where to look.\\" Investigators as a group must discard cards from their hands and/or play areas with a total of 6 {perPlayer} or more skill icons. Reduce this amount by 2 for each _Reporter_, _Detective_, and _Clairvoyant_ investigator chosen for this campaign.</li><li>\\"We don't have the time or resources to help.\\" Place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"whereToLook":"“You just have to know where to look.”","noTime":"“We don't have the time or resources to help.”"}},"behindTheCurtain":{"body":"<p>_Behind the Curtain:_ Out in a city as remote as Denver, you discover that the circus is being a little less careful with its illusory disguises. With the time you've gained, you can afford to watch for an opportunity to undo their spells and reveal their horrid deception to the public. The trick is making the deception plain for all to see.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"Time to show the city what they really are.\\" Investigators as a group must choose and discard 2 {perPlayer} total non-weakness assets they control. Reduce this amount by 1 for each _Sorcerer_, _Silver Twilight_, _Scholar_, and _Cultist_ investigator chosen for this campaign.</li><li>\\"We can't afford to stay here a moment longer.\\" Place 1 resource on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"showTheCity":"“Time to show the city what they really are.”","cantStay":"“We can't afford to stay here a moment longer.”"}},"humaneTreatment":{"body":"<p>_Humane Treatment:_ While you arrived in Denver far later than you wished to, there is still an advantage to be exploited. Student groups from several of the city's universities intend to boycott the circus on grounds of animal cruelty. While they don't truly grasp the evil truth of this particular circus, some creativity on your part may assist them in dissuading others from going to see the circus.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p><ul><li>\\"Give me that paint can and pasteboard.\\" Investigators as a group must choose and discard 3 {perPlayer} total non-weakness assets they control. Reduce this amount by 1 for each _Artist_, _Dreamer_, and _Miskatonic_ investigator chosen for this campaign.</li><li>\\"We can't afford to stay here a moment longer.\\" Place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li></ul>","label":{"paintCan":"“Give me that paint can and pasteboard.”","cantStay":"“We can't afford to stay here a moment longer.”"}}},"throughTheForestsVI":{},"throughTheForestsVII":{},"noFreeRides":{},"engineTrouble":{},"theGreatTrainHorror":{},"scheduleToKeep":{},"caboose":{},"locomotiveEngine":{},"boxcar":{},"flatcar":{},"gondolaCar":{},"stockCar":{},"tankCar":{},"coalHopperCar":{},"craneCar":{},"mailCar":{},"refrigeratorCar":{},"reinforcedCar":{"label":{"reduceDamage":"Reduce the damage dealt by that attack by 1","reduceHorror":"Reduce the horror dealt by that attack by 1"}},"circusEngine":{},"exoticAnimalCar":{},"performersCar":{},"carrieDykstra":{},"ralphDykstra":{},"loomingGoatspawn":{},"rampagingGoatspawn":{},"ravenousGoatspawn":{},"writhingGoatspawn":{},"newMoonStiltwalker":{},"newMoonTumbler":{},"focusedSabotage":{},"overloadedEngine":{},"ricketyRide":{},"resolutions":{"resolution1":{"title":"Resolution 1","body":"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> <i>With you and each of your companions out of commission, Ralph and Carrie make an emergency stop and throw their everything into defending while you recuperate. By the time you've driven off the attackers and recovered from your wounds, you are days behind schedule. All you can do is get back on the rails and hope it's not too late.</i></p><ul><li>For each act remaining in the act deck, place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution2":{"title":"Resolution 2","body":"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> <i>The performers riding the circus train finally manage to jam the wheels of your own train. Ralph and Carrie shout at you to brace for a crash as the locked wheels buck the train upward and send you careening off to the side of the tracks. You drag yourself from the wreckage, ready to defend yourself, but the circus train has moved on already. More than a day goes by before you can get word to the local railways to bring a crane, putting you woefully behind schedule in getting to Los Angeles.</i></p><ul><li>Place 2 resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution3":{"title":"Resolution 3","body":"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> <i>You breathe a sigh of relief as the circus train fades from view behind you. Ralph checks his watch as he finishes attending to the machinery. “Nice work back there. I think we'll get to Los Angeles just behind schedule, but not by much.” A little behind is more than acceptable, given the obstacles and perils you had to endure across the country. You return to the caboose to rest, watching the landscape from the back railing, bathed in the orange glow of the setting sun.</i></p><ul><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution4":{"title":"Resolution 4","body":"<p><b>Resolution 4:</b> <i>You breathe a sigh of relief as the circus train fades from view behind you. Ralph slows the train with several careful looks at the engine gauges. “That last fight nearly damaged the engine. Best not to push it, unless you want to walk the rest of the way.” Frustrating, but sensible. You return to the caboose to rest, watching the landscape from the back railing, bathed in the orange glow of the setting sun.</i></p><ul><li>Place 1 resource on the scenario reference card.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution5":{"title":"Resolution 5","body":"<p><b>Resolution 5:</b> <i>It's early morning when Carrie rouses you from sleep. The ever-present thrum of the train wheels has stopped, and the hissing steam of the cooling engine is all but finished. “We're in the yard outside La Grande station,” Carrie says gently, helping to grab your belongings. You clamber down the back steps to find Ralph waiting for you. “Well... I guess this is the end of the line. To be honest, I'm not sure if we could go any further with you if we wanted. After that journey... I'm already going to have nightmares.” He looks to his daughter, and Carrie rubs one of her arms, nodding with a rueful expression. “But you've got that strength to see it through. We're counting on you. Not just for our family, but for everybody's families. We'll see you back in Arkham, God willing.” Carrie gives you and Thea tense embraces in farewell, while Ralph just offers a handshake, both covering their fear as much as they can. You book into a modest hotel and collapse, still weary despite having slept through the night. You wonder how much Blake has prepared over the last week and a half, and just how much a difference your actions over the journey have made.</i></p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the ringmaster had X days to prepare</i>, where X is the number of resources on the scenario reference card.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Interlude: Written in Stone</b>.</li></ul>"}}}`),Oe={allPointsWest:n},Be=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,allPointsWest:n,default:Oe},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),s="Circus Ex Mortis",r="<h1>In the Shadow of the New Moon</h1><p>The New Moon Circus has come to Arkham for one night only &mdash; and missing person cases and mysterious deaths have followed it up the coast. <i>Circus Ex Mortis</i> is an eight-part fan-made campaign for <i>Arkham Horror: The Card Game</i>, designed by Tyler Gotch.</p>",h=[{title:"Moon Tokens",body:"@:circusExMortis.additionalRules.moonTokens"}],l={title:"Additional Rules: Moon Tokens",moonTokens:"<p class='basic'>This campaign introduces a new kind of chaos token: the moon ({'{'}moon{'}'}) token. During the <i>Circus Ex Mortis</i> campaign, the moon plays a significant role, and the moon token represents both the strength and severity of its strange influence.</p><ul><li>{'{'}moon{'}'} tokens revealed during a skill test have the following effect: “0. Seal this token on your investigator card and reveal another token.”</li><li>{'{'}moon{'}'} tokens sealed on your investigator card have no effect on their own, but some card effects may reference whether or not there is a {'{'}moon{'}'} token sealed on your investigator card, or the number of {'{'}moon{'}'} tokens sealed on your investigator card.</li><li>At the end of the round, for each {'{'}moon{'}'} token sealed on your investigator card, you must (choose one):<ul><li>That token stays sealed on your investigator card.</li><li>Take 1 damage or 1 horror. Then, release that token.</li></ul></li><li>A {'{'}moon{'}'} token revealed outside of a skill test has no effect on its own unless otherwise specified by a card effect.</li></ul>"},d={title:"Prologue",body:"<p class='center basic'><b>_{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk} COMING SOON – THE NEW MOON CIRCUS! {asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}_</b></p><p class='center basic'>Come and see the <b>greatest show</b> in the <b>world!</b></p><p class='center basic'><b>Death-defying</b> acrobatics! Feats of <b>supreme strength and skill!</b></p><p class='center basic'><b>A <b>menagerie</b> of the most <b>incredible</b> creatures alive!</b></p><p class='center basic'>Coming to your town <b>this Sunday! One night only!</b></p><p class='center basic'><b>_{asterisk}{asterisk} DON'T MISS THIS ONCE-IN-A-LIFETIME CHANCE! {asterisk}{asterisk}_</b></p><p><i>Sunday, August 26th, 1923. Arkham, Massachusetts.</i></p><p>The New Moon Circus had been the talk of the town for the better part of the week. Traveling circuses tended to visit bigger cities for potential profit alone, and few people in Arkham could find time or money to visit Boston, New York, or Philadelphia on a whim. While the circus typically didn't draw the attention of high society, even the French Hill elite began to joke about seeing the circus for a lark. You confess, you had some interest in the circus as well, but not for the popular reasons.</p><p>Minnie Klein of the Arkham Advertiser was the first one to bring the coincidences to your attention. You found Minnie waiting for you at Velma's Diner with her notepad in hand and a hungry look in her eyes – and it wasn't for the lunch specials. “Take a look at this,” she says, using her pencil like a teacher's pointer, “The New Moon Circus used to work the usual circuit in the south, hitting all the big cities like Atlanta and Jacksonville, and never going further north than Memphis. Then a month ago, the circus suddenly took off up the coast, and started working a bunch of podunk towns on the way north. Arkham's the biggest one they've hit since Savannah.”</p><p>You concede that there's probably something odd behind the circus's decision but you fail to see what about it has excited Minnie. She quickly elaborates. “Missing person cases <b>and</b> mysterious deaths in each town the New Moon Circus has visited at the time the circus was in town. And here's the kicker.” Minnie smiles proudly as she taps at the bottom of her pad. “The people who went to see the circus? Nobody can remember anything concrete about it. Two people who live three states away gave their local papers the exact same quote about their experience. How's that for fishy?”</p><p>Fishy enough to warrant your investigation at the very least. And so with tickets in hand and preparations made for any possible contingency, you set out for the circus. The evening is still bright owing to the time of year, but the full moon is already rising.</p>",addMoonTokens:"Add 3 {'{'}moon{'}'} tokens to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign."},c={title:"The Tarot Deck",body:"<p class='basic'>If investigators choose to use the Tarot Deck from the Return to the Circle Undone expansion, there is some thematic connection to the Circus Ex Mortis campaign. Investigators may choose to perform an 8-card Campaign Reading with these specific 8 cards, in this order: Magician, Hermit, Strength, Chariot, Devil, Temperance, Sun, Moon</p>",label:{performCampaignReading:"Perform Campaign Reading",performIndividualReadings:"Perform a tarot reading before each scenario instead"}},u={oneNightOnly:"One Night Only",thePrimrosePath:"The Primrose Path","harm'sWay":"Harm's Way",allPointsWest:"All Points West",piperAtTheGatesOfDawn:"Piper at the Gates of Dawn",bacchanalia:"Bacchanalia",redSunrise:"Red Sunrise",thousandToOne:"Thousand to One"},p={label:{endOfRoundQuestion:"A {'{'}moon{'}'} token is sealed on your investigator card. You must choose one:",keepSealed:"That token stays sealed on your investigator card",takeDamageAndRelease:"Take 1 damage. Then, release that token",takeHorrorAndRelease:"Take 1 horror. Then, release that token"}},m={sealMoonToken:"<span>Search the chaos bag for a {'{'}moon{'}'} token and seal it on your investigator card</span>",brokenCouplings:{placeBetween:"Place between {locationA} and {locationB}"},circusEncampment:{doneReleasingMoonTokens:"Done releasing moon tokens"}},y={cluesToSpend:"Clues to spend"},g={theRingmasterDoesNotSuspectYou:"The ringmaster does not suspect you.",theRingmasterHasHisEyeOnYou:"The ringmaster has his eye on you.",theInvestigatorsWereLostInTheArkhamWoods:"The investigators were lost in the Arkham woods.",theInvestigatorsBypassedTheIllusions:"The investigators bypassed the illusions.",groupsOfCitizensWereSavedFromTheCircus:"Groups of citizens saved from the circus",theRingmasterHadDaysToPrepare:"Days the ringmaster had to prepare",theInvestigatorsCouldNotEscapeTheCircus:"The investigators could not escape the circus.",theInvestigatorsClashedWithBlake:"The investigators clashed with Blake.",theInvestigatorsUnmaskedBlake:"The investigators unmasked Blake.",theInvestigatorsStruckDownBlake:"The investigators struck down Blake.",theInvestigatorsMustFollowTheCult:"The investigators must follow the cult.",theInvestigatorsDiscoveredTheRitualsLocation:"The investigators discovered the ritual's location.",theInvestigatorsDidNotArriveInTime:"The investigators did not arrive in time.",theCultRallies:"The cult rallies.",theInvestigatorsWereDevouredByTheThousandYoung:"The investigators were devoured by the thousand young.",theInvestigatorsEndedTheRitual:"The investigators ended the ritual.",shubNiggurathReignsOverAnEclipsedWorld:"Shub-Niggurath reigns over an eclipsed world.",shubNiggurathVanishedWithTheEclipse:"Shub-Niggurath vanished with the eclipse.",theProphecyWasFulfilled:"The prophecy was fulfilled.",theProphecyWasUnfulfilled:"The prophecy was unfulfilled.",destinies:"Destinies",theNewMoonCircusWasNeverSeenAgain:"The New Moon Circus was never seen again.",theNewMoonCircusMaySomedayReturn:"The New Moon Circus may someday return."},f={moonlitForestShadowedPath:"Moonlit Forest (Shadowed Path): take 1 horror unless you have a {'{'}moon{'}'} token sealed on your investigator card."},b={label:{takeMove:"Immediately take a move action",takeEvade:"Immediately take an evade action"}},w={label:{autoSucceed:"<span>Search the chaos bag for a {'{'}moon{'}'} token and seal it on your investigator card to automatically succeed</span>"}},v={label:{directDamage:"Deal 1 direct damage to that card",directHorror:"Deal 1 direct horror to that card"}},k={label:{reduceTokens:"<span>Attach Primordial Evils to the scenario reference card. Reduce the modifier of each {'{'}skull{'}'}, {'{'}cultist{'}'}, {'{'}tablet{'}'}, {'{'}elderThing{'}'}, and {'{'}moon{'}'} token by 1</span>",placeDoom:"Place 1 doom on the current agenda. This effect can cause the current agenda to advance"}},T={label:{drawTopCard:"Draw the top card of their deck",drawBottomCard:"Draw the bottom card of their deck"}},I={label:{releaseTokens:"Release up to 2 {'{'}moon{'}'} tokens sealed on cards they control"}},S={label:{spendAdditionalAction:"Spend 1 additional action",discardUntilEnemy:"After completing this action, discard cards from the top of the encounter deck until an enemy is discarded, and spawn it at your location"}},C={label:{spendCluesToAutoSucceed:"Spend clues as a group to automatically succeed",doNotSpendClues:"Do not spend {count} clues"}},A={label:{spendCluesToAutoSucceed:"Spend clues as a group to automatically succeed",doNotSpendClues:"Do not spend {count} clues"}},R={label:{chooseDamage:"How much damage will the group take to reduce the clue cost?"}},_={label:{chooseHorror:"How much horror will the group take to reduce the clue cost?"}},Ne={name:s,intro:r,specialRules:h,additionalRules:l,prologue:d,campaignReading:c,destiny:u,moonToken:p,label:m,illusoryLocus:y,key:g,tooltips:f,theBigTopThirdRing:b,endlessSpawn:w,lostAllControl:v,primordialEvils:k,amaltheaWeaverOracleOfMystery:T,invocationOfDiana:I,closeWatch:S,hiddenInPlainSight:C,underLockAndKey:A,clappedInIrons:R,hypnoticState:_},Le=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,additionalRules:l,amaltheaWeaverOracleOfMystery:T,campaignReading:c,clappedInIrons:R,closeWatch:S,default:Ne,destiny:u,endlessSpawn:w,hiddenInPlainSight:C,hypnoticState:_,illusoryLocus:y,intro:r,invocationOfDiana:I,key:g,label:m,lostAllControl:v,moonToken:p,name:s,primordialEvils:k,prologue:d,specialRules:h,theBigTopThirdRing:b,tooltips:f,underLockAndKey:A},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),P=JSON.parse(`{"tokens":{"easyStandard":{"skull":"-X, where X is half the number of Bystander cards in the victory display, rounded up.","cultist":"-3. If you have not moved this round, choose one: discard 1 card from your hand, or lose 1 resource.","tablet":"-3. If you have moved this round, choose one: discard 1 card from your hand, or lose 1 resource.","elderThing":"-2. If this test is failed, reveal a fury token."},"hardExpert":{"skull":"-X, where X is 1 more than half the number of Bystander cards in the victory display, rounded up.","cultist":"-4. If you have not moved this round, choose one: discard 1 card from your hand, or lose 1 resource.","tablet":"-4. If you have moved this round, choose one: discard 1 card from your hand, or lose 1 resource.","elderThing":"-4. If this test is failed, reveal a fury token."}},"escapeActFuryReveal":{"title":"Fury Token Revealed","moon":"Ignore this token and reveal another fury token.","north":"Put Camp Outskirts into play above the top Camp location, instead of resolving the effects on The Dark Young Stir... Return each fury token to the fury bag.","south":"Put Camp Outskirts into play below the bottom Camp location, instead of resolving the effects on The Dark Young Stir... Return each fury token to the fury bag.","west":"Put Camp Outskirts into play to the left of the leftmost Camp location, instead of resolving the effects on The Dark Young Stir... Return each fury token to the fury bag.","east":"Put Camp Outskirts into play to the right of the rightmost Camp location, instead of resolving the effects on The Dark Young Stir... Return each fury token to the fury bag."},"furyReveal":{"title":"Fury Token Revealed","moon":"Immediately reveal two additional fury tokens.","north":"<div><span>Each Towering Dark Young makes an immediate attack against each investigator at the location...</span><br><br><span>...directly above them.</span></div>","south":"<div><span>Each Towering Dark Young makes an immediate attack against each investigator at the location...</span><br><br><span>...directly below them.</span></div>","west":"<div><span>Each Towering Dark Young makes an immediate attack against each investigator at the location...</span><br><br><span>...directly to the left of them.</span></div>","east":"<div><span>Each Towering Dark Young makes an immediate attack against each investigator at the location...</span><br><br><span>...directly to the right of them.</span></div>"},"intro":{"title":"Scenario III: Harm's Way","body":"<p>When you slip back out of the ringmaster's trailer, ghastly growls and other less identifiable sounds rumble through the camp. You nearly flinch as a shadow sweeps across the moon, which leads your view to a worse spectacle. Four massive figures tower above the camp, large enough to be oak trees &mdash; and indeed resembling them in silhouette &mdash; but far more horrible. Like the smaller abominations you encountered in the woods, these things are a horrid jumble of tentacles, mouths, hooves, and horns. They writhe and roar dully with sluggish movements. Perhaps these monsters are rousing from sleep, which lends a little more urgency to the mission. Thea holds a hand over her mouth in shock, but soon lowers it with a shudder. Whether or not she's seen them in her visions before, this appears to be the first time in person. It goes without saying that you must plan how to proceed in finding and rescuing the captives.</p><ul><li>The investigators must decide (choose one):<ul><li>“The faster we get them out of here, the better.” Add a {'{'}cultist{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>“Caution first. Saving them won’t help otherwise.” Add a {'{'}tablet{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li></ul></li></ul>","label":{"faster":"“The faster we get them out of here, the better.”","caution":"“Caution first. Saving them won’t help otherwise.”"}},"setup":{"gatherSets":"Gather all cards from the <i>Harm's Way</i>, <i>Cult of Shub-Niggurath</i>, <i>Lunatic Night</i>, <i>New Moon Entertainers</i>, and <i>Panicked Masses</i> encounter sets. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/040.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/cult-of-shub-niggurath.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/lunatic-night.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/new-moon-entertainers.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/sets/panicked-masses.png' /></section>","placeLocations":"Randomly choose two of the four copies of Crowded Row and Secluded Tent and remove them from the game. Put the remaining copies into play along with the Ringmaster's Trailer location.","startAt":"Each investigator begins play at Ringmaster's Trailer.","toweringDarkYoung":"Randomly choose one of the five copies of Towering Dark Young and remove it from the game. Put the remaining four copies into play at each corner of the map, not at any location.","furyBag":"Create a separate bag consisting of a {cultist}, {tablet}, {skull}, and {elderThing} token. This is the fury bag, and these are fury tokens. They are not chaos tokens. This bag will be used during the scenario by other cards.","darkYoungStir":"Put the Dark Young Stir... story card into play next to the fury bag.","kidnappedCitizens":"Randomly choose two of the six copies of Kidnapped Citizen and remove them from the game. Put the remaining four copies into play at different copies of Crowded Row and Secluded Tent.","checkCampaignLogIllusions":"Check the Campaign Log:","bypassedTheIllusions":"If <i>the investigators bypassed the illusions</i>, the ringmaster will notice your earlier meddling and be back sooner. Place 2 doom on agenda 1a. This doom ignores the forced effect.","lostInTheArkhamWoods":"If <i>the investigators were lost in the Arkham woods</i>, the illusory wards are still in place. No changes are made.","checkCampaignLogAct":"Check the Campaign Log:","eyeOnYou":"If <i>the ringmaster has his eye on you</i>, for this scenario, use “Act 1 &ndash; Escape Act (v.I).” Remove the other copy of act 1 from the game.","doesNotSuspectYou":"If <i>the ringmaster does not suspect you</i>, for this scenario, use “Act 1 &ndash; Escape Act (v.II).” Remove the other copy of act 1 from the game.","setAside":"Set each copy of Camp Outskirts aside, out of play.","startingCards":"The investigators with Amalthea Weaver and De Cultus Bestiae in their decks may begin the game with those cards in their opening hands as additional cards."},"startingCards":{"instructions":"The investigators with Amalthea Weaver and De Cultus Bestiae in their decks may begin the game with those cards in their opening hands as additional cards.","label":{"take":"Begin with this card as an additional card in your opening hand","leave":"Leave this card in your deck"}},"escapeActVI":{},"escapeActVII":{},"overdueDeparture":{},"theCircusSleeps":{},"treadingOnEggshells":{},"sleepWhenYoureDead":{"label":{"physicalTrauma":"Suffer 1 physical trauma","mentalTrauma":"Suffer 1 mental trauma"}},"theDarkYoungStir":{},"hiddenInPlainSight":{},"underLockAndKey":{},"cautiousJailers":{},"deepInTheDark":{},"clappedInIrons":{},"hypnoticState":{},"resolutions":{"resolution1":{"title":"Resolution 1","body":"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> Overwhelmed by the threats lurking in the circus camp, you retreat into the woods, hoping that the illusions to keep intruders out of the camp will at least speed you away from the horrid site. By the time you gather your wits and shake off the injuries you've sustained, the moon is setting, and the first glow of dawn begins to saturate the woods. You trudge wearily back toward Arkham with the few captives you managed to keep close to you in your flight.</p><ul><li>Remove 2 copies of Kidnapped Citizen from the victory display, if possible. In your Campaign Log, record that <i>X groups of citizens were saved from the circus</i>, where X is the number of Kidnapped Citizens in the victory display.</li><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution2":{"title":"Resolution 2","body":"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> Your escape from the circus camp is a slow and quiet affair, and you do not breathe easily until the woods begin to thin and the outermost buildings of Arkham are visible in the pre-dawn light. The grateful citizens shed tears of relief, thanking you up and down for your heroic efforts in saving them. Your appreciation is muddled by the civilians all agreeing that beyond the circus performers and their animals, it was only the night playing tricks on them. Many of them have repressed the horrors, and are eager to leave them behind without another thought.</p><p>While you suppose the safety of the citizens was priority, it will be on your shoulders once again to discover just what deeper mysteries the circus is hiding. There is more at work than wanton murder, that much is certain.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>X groups of citizens were saved from the circus</i>, where X is the number of Kidnapped Citizens in the victory display.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution3":{"title":"Resolution 3","body":"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> After sending off the rescued victims and urging them to inform the police of last night's events, you are left with only Thea. There is still much to discuss of her visions and the stolen tome, and you invite her to enlighten you after you've both had some sorely-needed rest.</p><p>You sleep deeply through the morning, assured at least a little that the circus won't attack you in broad daylight in the heart of Arkham with their horrors in tow. Restful as it is, your dreams flash with the vivid imagery of the previous night. The circus. The grinning ringmaster. The moon. Those creatures. The forest. Voices. Chanting. Terror. You awaken with a sudden surge of adrenaline, but find nothing but the stillness of your own bedroom.</p><p>Thea is still fitfully asleep as you step out to visit the police. In the hours since your return, the public outcry forced a full investigation of the circus. Frustratingly &ndash; and predictably, perhaps &ndash; the police found nothing but trampled mud at the circus grounds, and even the few willing officers they sent into the woods reported only an abandoned campsite. Naturally they promised to keep on the case, but without anything immediate to chase, you expect that the New Moon Circus will be filed away in their cold case cabinets.</p><p>Once again the burden falls to you, but where to start? The only trace of the circus left in town are the posters that drew the public in to begin with. You find the nearest one that hasn't been torn down by traumatized citizens and inspect it.</p><p>While you expected another dead-end, you make a startling discovery at the bottom of the poster.</p><p class='center'><b>{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk} WITH SPECIAL MATINÉES AT {asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}</b></p><p class='center'><b>CHICAGO &ndash; Aug. 29 &#124; ST. LOUIS &ndash; Sept. 2</b></p><p class='center'><b>DENVER &ndash; Sept. 5 &#124; LOS ANGELES &ndash; Sept. 9</b></p><p class='center'><b>{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk} DON'T MISS YOUR CHANCE! {asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}{asterisk}</b></p><p>You couldn't have found a better roadmap if you planned it. There's no way to confirm if this schedule still holds true after the events last night, but from what little you know of Sylvester Blake, he's not the type to do anything halfway, nor keep an audience waiting.</p><p>Plans form and crumble in your head as you return to your home, but nothing has cemented by the time you arrive. You enter to find Thea at your kitchen table, studying Blake's tome carefully. She nearly jumps with surprise, but gives a relieved smile at the sight of you. “Mercy... I keep expecting something horrible after all those months.” Thea gestures to a telegram on the table that arrived while you were out &ndash; from Minnie Klein, your newspaper contact.</p><p>You've barely picked up the message when a knock sounds firmly at the door, startling both you and Thea. You open it cautiously, but find a broad man in dark blue work clothes with his cap in hand, with a young lady in similar clothes beside him. “I um... hope this is a good time,” he says with clear lack of practice with polite conversation. “You don't know me, but my boy told me that you saved his life after he snuck off to the circus last night. I'm Ralph Dykstra, engineer with the Old Colony Railroad. This is my daughter, Carrie.”</p><p>The young woman crosses her arms with a wry expression. “I'm your brakewoman, dad.” The engineer returns her look, but continues. “I'm a man who pays his debts, and if you need anything, I'll arrange it.” Even after insisting on the danger at your heels, Ralph and Carrie remain firm in helping you. Perhaps Thea is onto something with her talk of fate and prophecy. You take the folded circus poster from your pocket and glance between it and Minnie's telegram, deciding which course of action to take.</p><ul><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>The investigators may choose to play the <i>Curse of the Rougarou</i> side-story immediately after this scenario. If they do, it costs each investigator 1 fewer experience. Some gameplay may be altered.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario IV: All Points West</b>.</li></ul>"}}}`),He={harmsWay:P},je=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:He,harmsWay:P},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),E={title:"Interlude: The Future and the Past",intro:"<p>The door to the ringmaster's trailer thankfully opens and closes with barely any sound. Its interior is lavishly furnished, every piece of furniture and decor made from material of the finest quality. One shelf is stocked with books of the occult, the very writing on their spines already sparking a feeling of dread in you. Your browsing has only begun when a quiet sound snaps your attention to a dark curtain separating the trailer into halves. Cautiously, you ready yourself for trouble and throw back the curtain.</p><p>The second half is no less richly decorated, but hardly worthy of your attention. A dark-skinned woman in the garb of a fortune teller sits bound to a chair and gagged, softly stirring in an exhausted state. Her eyes drift up to you, weary at first, but widen in shock in an instant. The woman leans forward, her breathing accelerating as you reach back to untie the knotted cloth. “It's you!” she gasps quietly, her voice dry but still smooth with a southern drawl, “from my visions! It's... it's really happening!”</p>",farSeeing:{title:"Far-Seeing",body:"<p><i>If 1 or more Clairvoyant investigators were chosen for this campaign, those investigators read Far-Seeing.</i></p><p>You're no stranger to glimpses of the future, but you're more accustomed to seeing rather than being seen. Knowing that you play some part in this woman's visions lends a new perspective to your own.</p><p class='basic'>You earn 1 bonus experience, which can only be used to purchase <i>Augury</i> cards.</p>"},xp:{farSeeing:"Far-Seeing"},thea:"<p>Thea shudders as she thinks back. “He forced me to tell him of my visions. Not physically, but my mind... he used his magic to squeeze it like an orange, make me talk about things I didn't even know that I knew... It took all my strength just to hold back the details of who could stop him... only that you were here, in Arkham, but that was my only hope... and y'all are a wonderful sight for sore eyes.”</p><p>It's a lot to take in at once. Whether or not you believe Thea's story, Blake still brought the circus north to Arkham pursuing those who saw against him. He'll be after your blood, especially with your actions trying to stop his slaughter at the very least. You ask Thea if she knows just what Blake wants to stop your involvement in, and she gives a dazed nod. “I don't fully know, but let me show you something. I'm sure I can help you figure it out.”</p>",addAmaltheaWeaver:"One investigator must add Amalthea Weaver (Circus Fortune Teller) to their deck. This card does not count toward that investigator's deck size.",theTome:"<p>Recovering her strength by degrees, Thea directs you back to the first half of the trailer, to the shelf of occult books. “That one, with the light brown leather,” she indicates. You pull the weathered tome from its place and inspect the cover. Eldritch symbols adorn the cover, but nothing distinguishes it from the other works near it. You unlatch the clasp and inspect the aged parchment inside.</p>",linguaFranca:{title:"Lingua Franca",body:"<p><i>If 1 or more Miskatonic, Scholar or Believer investigators were chosen for this campaign, those investigators read Lingua Franca.</i></p><p>Despite its age, the penmanship is clear and the words recognizable. You have a familiarity with Latin, due to your own upbringing, and can understand it easily. If this tome is important, your task is just a little simpler now.</p><p class='basic'>You begin the next scenario with 1 additional card in your opening hand.</p>"},apuleius:"<p>Thea stands beside you as you study the first page of the old tome. “So this is it. Blake would often have this book in hand when he questioned me.” Her finger traces a word at the top of the page. “Apuleius,” she mutters. You ask Thea how much she can read of the tome. “Most of it. One of the magicians at the old circus taught me to read and write Latin. They said that knowing it would add some flair to my fortune telling. Seems so long ago now...” You close the book and add it to your belongings. There will be time to study its secrets later, but you have to get out of Blake's hands.</p>",addDeCultusBestiae:"One investigator must add De Cultus Bestiae (Forgotten Work of Apuleius) to their deck. This card does not count toward that investigator's deck size.",eclipse:"<p>You wonder aloud what the ancient text and Thea's visions have in common, and Thea wrings her hands together. “There's one other thing from my visions I can see there's... an eclipse. A full one.”</p>",likeClockwork:{title:"Like Clockwork",body:"<p><i>If Norman Withers was chosen for this campaign, that investigator reads Like Clockwork.</i></p><p>The astronomical community has long held predictive models for the motions of the sun and moon. Though stars are more your specialty, the topic has jogged some academic memories that you had shelved until now.</p><p class='basic'>Your deckbuilding options gain “Up to 2 additional Seeker cards (&loz;) level 1-2.”</p>"},escape:"<p>A total eclipse. The celestial event is certainly mystic in itself, but its exact importance to Sylvester Blake and his circus isn't clear. The answers must be somewhere in the leatherbound tome, but you can't devote time to study it here now. You ask Thea to think on her visions once you're safely away from the encampment with as many captive civilians as you can find. She agrees and readies herself for a cautious bid for freedom. It's now that you wish the full moon would vanish for a while to help cover the escape.</p>",addMoonToken:"Add a {'{'}moon{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign."},M={title:"Interlude: Written in Stone",intro:"<p>A knock sounds at the door to your room, erasing any weariness from your mind. You open it cautiously, but find Thea – her own room directly across the hall from yours – with the tome held to her chest. You usher her inside quickly and lock the door. “I didn't really have a chance during the journey, but I have to talk with y'all about what I learned from this book.”</p><p>“The book – De Cultus Bestiae – was written by Apuleius, who lived in the Roman Empire. He was a scholar and poet, and he dabbled in several cults. Normally that would be cults in the old sense, like specific parts of the Roman pantheon, but this account is specifically about the cult of... Shub-Niggurath.”</p><p>The tome details the cult of Shub-Niggurath – disguised as a cult of Bacchus – and how Apuleius infiltrated it, learned their secrets, and aided the local Roman governor in dissolving the cult in that region. Most of the horrors are known to you through your recent trials, but Thea goes on to explain several key revelations.</p><p>“He claims that Shub-Niggurath can be summoned by a ritual in a forest during any new moon, but only temporarily. The cult back in that time was devising a ritual to permanently summon their god by locking the moon in place during an eclipse, but their works were burned when the cult was scattered. The high priest laid out a prophecy before his execution, which Apuleius recorded in the tome.”</p><p>Thea shows you a passage which she translates as she reads. “By the cunning of the Lord of the Woods, consort of the Mother Goddess, the words will once more be known, her mighty young fattened, and the stars of the black sky be aligned. Red will be the dawn and red the forest when neither moon nor sun shine down again. Iä! Shub-Niggurath! The Goat with a Thousand Young!”</p>",prophecy:"<p>Thea swallows dryly as she completes the passage. “I know how he felt now. That prophecy is immediately followed up by a short protective prayer to Diana, the Roman goddess of wild animals, the hunt, and the moon.” She again shows you the book, this time saying the Latin phrase aloud.</p>",addInvocationOfDiana:"Each investigator may add a copy of Invocation of Diana to their deck. These cards do not count toward those investigators' deck size.",destinyIntro:"<p>You ask Thea if that's all there is to the prophecy, because that doesn't explain why Blake was worried about your involvement. “It's actually two prophecies together rather than one,” Thea explains, turning to a later page in the book. “Apuleius consulted the high priestess of Diana following the execution, and she gave her own prophecy of hope – of those who would rise to stop it.”</p><p class='basic'>Each investigator must choose one of the following options. Then, in the Campaign Log under “Destinies,” record that investigator's name and the chosen word. Each investigator must choose a different option. If an investigator is killed or driven insane, their destiny is transferred to the investigator chosen to replace them.</p>",role:"<p>Thea reads out the translated descriptions of these foreseen figures and you must admit, you do fit the model. Granted you're not sure if a priestess from nearly two millennia ago could see you specifically, but it's as likely as all the other improbable things that happened in the past two weeks. Thea's expression grows a little uncertain as she looks between you and the text. “Y'all are there, plain to see, but... I just wish I knew what there was still in store for me. If this whole thing is true, then my visions were just to get y'all involved in it, and now... well, is that for it?”</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",determination:"<p><b>Determination:</b> You argue that the prophecy was peeping through the keyhole of time. Just because she wasn't in the small visible part doesn't mean she isn't there and making a huge difference. “Take for example, where did the prophecy talk about them and their instrumental part in getting you here?” Thea exhales and looks visibly relieved. “Y'all are right. I've got to take matters into my own hands and believe that what I'm doing makes a difference. Y'all were doing that before you even knew about any prophecies.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Aspirant of Courage).</p>",guidance:"<p><b>Guidance:</b> You argue that perhaps her visions are an extension of the same prophecy. The ancient priestess could only see and understand so much, so perhaps it's up to Thea to complete the rest. Her ability and knowledge have allowed you to understand this ages old prophecy in the first place, after all. Thea looks down at the book in her hands, nodding quietly. “Y'all are right. I've got to stop thinking about my visions in such a narrow window. There's got to be more to them, if only I focus on understanding them.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Aspirant of Wisdom).</p>",furtherReading:{title:"Further Reading",body:"<p>Thea turns back to the page with the profane declaration and furls her brow in contemplation. “I just wish we knew what Blake was planning. He seems to have everything he needs for this prophecy, and he only needed to come to California for this eclipse, so why go out of his way to hunt you down? He's just so certain of these prophecies and his visions, but why?”</p>"},noChoice:{title:"No Choice",body:"<p><i>If 1 or more Chosen investigators were chosen for this campaign, read No Choice.</i></p><p>You can't begin to understand a mind as twisted and evil as Blake's, but as someone who accepted your place in events long ago, you have a little insight into his fixation.</p><p class='basic'>You may heal 1 physical or mental trauma.</p>"},motive:"<p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",fanaticism:"<p><b>Fanaticism:</b> You suggest that since Blake serves Shub-Niggurath, this ritual is millennia in the making. He would rather die than allow the cult to fail a second time, and as such he would follow the tome of Apuleius to the letter in his task.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Interpretation of Conviction).</p>",nemesis:"<p><b>Nemesis:</b> You suggest that for a man as confident and prepared as Blake is, your presence in the prophecy represents more than simple prose. Your theft of Apuleius' tome also likely has a personal aspect to his situation, and helps drive his existing vendetta against you.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Interpretation of Obsession).</p>",bookmark:"<p><b>Bookmark:</b> There's no end to the theories you could imagine about the prophecies and Blake. What you've supposed is just as likely to be true as not, after all. You and Thea agree to shelve these thoughts as you apply your brains to the more immediate problems.</p>",addSkullToken:"Add a {'{'}skull{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.",label:{addInvocationOfDianaQuestion:"You may add a copy of Invocation of Diana to your deck. It does not count toward your deck size.",addInvocationOfDiana:"Add Invocation of Diana to your deck",doNotAddInvocationOfDiana:"Do not add Invocation of Diana",determination:'"Prophecy can only happen if people like you take action."',guidance:'"Perhaps you have a similar role to the Priestess of Diana."',healTraumaQuestion:"No Choice: You may heal 1 physical or mental trauma.",healPhysicalTrauma:"Heal 1 physical trauma",healMentalTrauma:"Heal 1 mental trauma",doNotHealTrauma:"Do not heal trauma",fanaticism:`"Maybe he's so dedicated that literally nothing else matters."`,nemesis:'"Maybe we just represent failure to him personally."',destinyQuestion:"Choose one of the following destinies:",heart:'"The one who will strike the heart."',pipes:'"The one who will silence the pipes."',torch:'"The one who will raise the torch."',rock:'"The one who will split the rock."',sigil:'"The one who will scribe the sigil."',stain:'"The one who will cleanse the stain."',prayer:'"The one who will recite the prayer."',burden:'"The one who will bear the burden."'}},x={title:"Interlude: Good Omens",destinyReminder:"<p>Each card in this interlude can be found in the <i>Destiny and Prophecy</i> encounter set, indicated by this icon:</p>",intro:"<p>The first rays of sunlight begin to warm the city as you begin your journey northward. Thea is focused intently on the final page of Apuleius' account, mouthing the Latin words and lingering on each one. After a long pause, she finally turns toward you...</p>",moreToDo:"<p><b>More to Do:</b> “I've been trying to control my visions more directly. It's been working, but there's just... too many of them. I lose the details if I try to take it all in. How would y'all decide which visions are the most important ones?”</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",priorWarning:"<p><b>Prior Warning:</b> Thea nods, folding the book with a serene smile. “I'll do exactly that. Even though I'm the one supposed to be guiding you, you've given me plenty of guidance. But it's my turn for sure now. We'll be ready for anything they can cook up.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Oracle of Purity).</p>",sawItComing:"<p><b>Saw it Coming:</b> Thea nods, shutting the book with a brave smile. “I'll do exactly that. Even though I'm the one supposed to be guiding you, you've given me plenty of guidance. But it's my turn for sure now. They won't be able to twitch without us knowing it.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Oracle of Resolve).</p>",moreToSee:"<p><b>More to See:</b> “I've been trying to open myself up to my visions more, let them play out fully and reveal things I didn't see before. I just... don't know how to interpret them. What would y'all do with the visions and the prophecies?”</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",writtenInInk:"<p><b>Written in Ink:</b> Thea casts her eyes back toward the tome. “I'll do exactly that. Even though I'm the one supposed to be guiding you, you've given me plenty of guidance. But it's my turn for sure now. We'll make sure this prophecy goes exactly to plan.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Oracle of Enlightenment).</p>",writtenInSmoke:"<p><b>Written in Smoke:</b> Thea casts her eyes back toward the tome. “I'll do exactly that. Even though I'm the one supposed to be guiding you, you've given me plenty of guidance. But it's my turn for sure now. We'll make sure that destiny is in our hands.”</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck swaps her with Amalthea Weaver (Oracle of Mystery).</p>",theLastWord:{title:"The Last Word",body:"<p>Your own thoughts stray to the old tome, and you wonder aloud just what the cult knows that you don't. After all, the tome was in Blake's possession for who knows how many years.</p>"},theInfinite:"<p><b>The Infinite:</b> If you're right in Blake's devotion being his driving motivation, then his followers will put their effort into the ritual foremost, and rely on the foul spell to carry them to victory.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",powersAbove:"<p><b>Powers Above:</b> The tome has guided you this far, in a sense, and you see no reason to deviate from that now. The incantations of the book will be needed now more than ever.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Prophecy of the Beyond).</p>",powersBelow:"<p><b>Powers Below:</b> The tome has guided you this far, in a sense, but not without your own talents carrying it along. Cautious use of the book will be the wisest course of action this morning.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Prophecy of the Eternal).</p>",theEndless:"<p><b>The Endless:</b> If you're right in Blake's vengeance being his driving motivation, then his followers will rely on the physical agents of their god, the goatspawn and the malignant dark young for victory.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must decide (choose one):</p>",againstTheFlood:"<p><b>Against the Flood:</b> Shub-Niggurath is named in the tome as the black goat of a thousand young, and you must expect to face and defeat countless enemies before the day is out.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Prophecy of the Horde).</p>",againstTheStorm:"<p><b>Against the Storm:</b> You have seen many times the sheer size and power of the greatest of Shub-Niggurath's children, and you will have to do everything in your power to oppose them today.</p><p class='basic'>The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck swaps it with De Cultus Bestiae (Prophecy of the Behemoth).</p>",breakOfDawn:"<p><b>Break of Dawn:</b> You and Thea share quiet, if tired, conversation as you proceed north out of Los Angeles in the growing daylight. The clear sky does little to assuage your worries of the coming fight.</p>",addSkullToken:"Add a {'{'}skull{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.",label:{priorWarning:'"Focus on using the visions to keep us protected."',sawItComing:'"Focus on using the visions to fight these monsters."',writtenInInk:'"Try to square the visions with the written prophecy."',writtenInSmoke:'"Take the visions as they are, beyond the prophecy."',powersAbove:'"We must rely on forces beyond humanity for guidance."',powersBelow:'"We must rely on our own strengths in this fight."',againstTheFlood:'"We must prepare to face thousands."',againstTheStorm:'"We must prepare to face giants."'}},D={title:"Epilogue",intro:"<p><i>Read the following only if the investigators won the campaign.</i></p><p>With the possibility of the Liber Pater Society waiting for you back in Los Angeles with plans of vengeance, you instead depart the redwood forest northward toward San Francisco. Your harrowing experience has left you wary of forests in general, and you welcome the train ride back across open country.</p>",underWraps:{title:"Under Wraps",body:"<p><i>If an investigator has Monstrous Transformation in their deck, that investigator reads Under Wraps.</i></p><p>The savage urges have been largely subdued since the battle under the eclipse, but you know that this is something you will have to contend with constantly, perhaps for the rest of your life. Until you discover a cure for the curse of the Rougarou, there will have to be blood, one way or another.</p>"},divergingPaths:{title:"Diverging Paths",body:"<p><i>If an investigator has Lady Esprit in their deck, that investigator reads Diverging Paths.</i></p><p>Lady Esprit has kept a more aloof mood than usual since the ordeal in the redwood forest. By the time your journey reaches St. Louis once again, the bokor remains on the platform as you board the train to Chicago. “Papa Legba stands at the crossroads and points the way where I'm needed most. But don't you worry none. If you need me, then the roads will lead me to you once again.”</p>"},thea:"<p>Thea has remained a constant – if quiet – companion for the journey back to Arkham. Since Blake's acquisition of the Four Leaf Circus, Thea's life had been funneled toward the eclipse ritual. Everything had built to that moment, and now she is adrift. Even Thea's visions don't suggest any distinct events to come. Her future is an open book, so to speak, though she still keeps a close hand on De Cultus Bestiae.</p>",kernelOfTruth:{title:"Kernel of Truth",body:"<p><i>If the prophecy was fulfilled:</i></p><p>Thea rubs a hand smoothly on the weathered cover of the tome. “It's strange to think of all those ancient folks putting such trust in us. Neither the priestess nor Apuleius really knew what the cult was doing or how it could be stopped, but they just... hoped. I suppose I do know that hope, at least.”</p><p class='basic'>Each investigator earns 2 bonus experience for realizing their part in events beyond true understanding.</p>"},xp:{kernelOfTruth:"Kernel of Truth"},grainOfSalt:{title:"Grain of Salt",body:"<p><i>If the prophecy was unfulfilled:</i></p><p>Thea holds the tome with both hands, contemplating it like a headstone. “I don't know what the priestess really did and didn't see, but I think it served its purpose. Even if all those flowery words did was getting you to that forest, then it doesn't really matter what was truth and what was just hope. I can't blame the priestess for wanting a future beyond the cult's ambitions.”</p>"},lookingAhead:{title:"Looking Ahead",body:"<p>While the both of you close this somewhat literal chapter of your lives, the question of the future still remains. You ask Thea what she intends to do if she accompanies you all the way to Arkham. “I'm still trying to figure that part out. I don't think I can just go back to the circus life after everything that's happened. If I still get visions that are even half as important as the ones with you and Blake, they'll be more than circus admission price. Though I suppose I've still got to eat in the meantime.”</p><p>You suggest introducing Thea to some of your allies in Arkham, such as Dr. Henry Armitage. With her proficiency in Latin – and more experience in occult matters than anyone could reasonably hope – Thea would be a boon to the Miskatonic Library. The fortune teller's eyes drift to the train window, gazing over the rushing landscape with a wistful expression. “Never know until I try, right?”</p><p>Your return to Arkham is met with very little fanfare at all. The circus is all but forgotten – in many cases – as the citizens seek any normalcy they can find in this town. Ralph and Carrie Dykstra catch sight of you at the Northside platform and eagerly reunite with offers of congratulations. Minnie Klein is soon to follow, eager to harvest the fruit of the journalistic seeds she planted. She knows full well that her editor Doyle Jeffries won't print a word of this, but her own curiosity is satisfied if nothing else. The two brief meetings are more meaningful than anyone around you can guess, but without your experiences, hardly enough to draw a glance.</p><p>Thea departs for Southside with plenty of thankful goodbyes, seeking a temporary room at Ma's boarding house until she can settle on a new situation, and leaving you alone for the first time in nearly a month.</p>"},restAssured:{title:"Rest Assured",body:"<p>You walk the familiar roads to your home in Rivertown, enjoying the brief respite in the cool September air. Arkham is gloomy even in the best of weather, making it the perfect climate for the many subtle and insidious evils that lurk throughout. You're almost glad of evils that instead present themselves colorfully as a poisonous reptile. Had a plot like this developed in total secrecy, there would have been little hope of uncovering the truth. It's a reminder to be vigilant, and to never take events at face value. There's a sucker born every minute, the circus saying goes.</p><p class='basic'>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the New Moon Circus was never seen again</i>.</p>"},encore:{title:"Encore",body:"<p>You walk the familiar roads to your home in Rivertown, enjoying the brief respite in the cool September air. It gives you time to think on the past events, particularly those surrounding Sylvester Blake himself. Despite your victory in the forest, Blake disappeared without a trace, and you're certain you haven't seen the last of him. The ringmaster is as vindictive as he is cunning, and you had better watch your back as long as there's any chance of his reappearance. It may or may not be in the guise of the New Moon Circus, but evil wears many faces.</p><p class='basic'>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the New Moon Circus may someday return</i>. The investigator with Amalthea Weaver in their deck must add a copy of The Tower &bull; XVI to their deck. The investigator with De Cultus Bestiae in their deck must add a copy of The Devil &bull; XV to their deck.</p>"}},Fe={theFutureAndThePast:E,writtenInStone:M,goodOmens:x,epilogue:D},ze=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:Fe,epilogue:D,goodOmens:x,theFutureAndThePast:E,writtenInStone:M},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),W={intro:{title:"Scenario I: One Night Only",body:`<p>The woods south of Uptown loom above you in the fading light as you approach the circus grounds. Smiling barkers take your tickets and usher you in with enthusiastic shouts of the many waiting attractions, though you only take note of potential threats. If this circus is harboring dark and deadly things, then you can't afford to let your guard down for even a moment. You follow the flow of the crowd to the main tent, wondering where trouble might start.</p><p>With a sudden loud fanfare, a long parade of exotic animals and costumed acrobats snakes around the tent, each settling in their performance areas to the applause of the crowd. A tall man &ndash; unnaturally tall &ndash; with a pointed beard and a pitch-black suit saunters between the three rings and gives an elegant bow to the audience. You catch an unsettling glint in his eyes as he raises his head to address the cheering citizens.</p><p><i>"Ladies and gentlemen, boys and girls, welcome to the greatest spectacle of your lives! Watch in amazement as I, Sylvester Blake, ringmaster of the New Moon Circus, unveil our most impossible trick!"</i> The ringmaster's voice booms out, but with a tone just as unnatural as his appearance. He weaves his hands through the air with a magician's deftness, and one of the elephants rears up with a trumpet call. Cheers and applause ring out from the audience as the elephant repeats its motion, but its call grows distorted and its form begins to waver. When the animal rises for a third time, its head begins to split, and its cry is utterly alien. The crowd's cheering gives way to horrified screams, and pandemonium breaks.</p>`,behindTheCurtain:"<p><b>Behind the Curtain:</b> <i>As you seat yourself in the bleachers, eyes instinctively stray to where the performers gather before beginning their routines. The few visible members scan the room furtively, practicing strange hand motions.</i></p><p>You begin the game with 1 clue from the token bank.</p>"},seats:{label:{firstRing:`"I'll take a seat next to the animal acts." You begin play at The Big Top (First Ring).`,secondRing:`"I'll take a seat next to the acrobats." You begin play at The Big Top (Second Ring).`,thirdRing:`"I'll take a seat next to the clowns." You begin play at The Big Top (Third Ring).`}},houseOfHorrors:{label:{discardHalfHand:"Discard half the cards in your hand (rounded up)",sealMoonToken:"<span>Search the chaos bag for a {'{'}moon{'}'} token and seal it on your investigator card</span>"}},mesmericMagic:{label:{physicalTrauma:"Suffer 1 physical trauma",mentalTrauma:"Suffer 1 mental trauma"}},resolutions:{noResolution:{title:"No Resolution",body:"<p>_If no resolution was reached (each investigator was defeated):_ Read _Resolution 1_."},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> The rough scraping of the ground beneath your body and the sounds of woodland nightlife rouse you slowly but surely back to consciousness. You open one eye groggily to find one of the circus performers dragging you through the woods further south of Arkham. Though it came at the price of a welt on the back of your head, you&rsquo;re outside that accursed circus and free from the illusory influence.</p><p>You summon your strength and send a wild strike into one of your captor&rsquo;s kidneys, causing him to drop you with an outcry of pain. You push yourself quickly upright, ready to fight for your freedom if need be. The carnie sizes you up, ready for another fight, but looks up at the full moon above you both. With a grimace, he turns and runs deeper into the woods behind him at a breakneck pace, far more nimbly than you would have suspected at a glance. You doubt you could catch up to him in the treacherous Arkham woods, but you at least know that he has other priorities now.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the ringmaster does not suspect you</i>.</li><li>If it was act 1 when the game ended, look at the back of the act 1 chosen for the scenario and add the listed token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> You tread swiftly out onto the dry dirt path leading up to the circus, with dozens of frightened survivors close behind you. Well clear of the carnage and kidnapping for the moment, you advise the crowd to return to Arkham as fast as they can and inform the police. The Arkham brass aren&rsquo;t the most reliable, but even the magic tricks of the circus won&rsquo;t be able to cover this one up.</p><p>As the victims return to safety, your thoughts turn back to the circus still looming behind you. What was it all for? People capable of controlling those horrid beasts and wielding hypnotic magic wouldn&rsquo;t organize all this just out of pure malice. Considering Minnie&rsquo;s report of their sudden trek north to Arkham as well, there has to be some deliberate purpose behind the chaos tonight, but what?</p><p>The ringmaster &mdash; Sylvester Blake &mdash; is sure to have the answers to everything. A man of his stark and menacing appearance shouldn&rsquo;t be hard to lose track of, but he disappeared shortly after the chaos began. Likely more of the circus illusions at work. Does he not want to do his own dirty work, or does he have other reasons for staying aloof? Time will tell, as you intend to confront the man yet.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the ringmaster has his eye on you</i>.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"Resolution 3",body:"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> A nearby scream sends a jolt of adrenaline through your system once more, and you advance into the treeline. A young boy struggles in the grip of another circus performer &mdash; a thin man with angular features &mdash; who is attempting to drag him possibly deeper into the woods. A twig cracks under your foot in the approach, and the abductor snaps his head up toward you for barely a second before he abandons his prey and retreats into the forest. The boy scrabbles back against a tree, and only once you introduce yourself calmly does he visibly settle. You tell him to get back to Arkham without delay, and he does, only giving a mumbled thank you as he runs off.</p><p>One down, dozens to go. You turn your attention back to the moonlit trees. Most people avoid the Arkham woods during the day, to say nothing of its dangers at night, but you have little choice. The circus performers must have kidnapped dozens of people during the bedlam. If you don&rsquo;t rescue the victims tonight, before the circus has a chance to leave, then they&rsquo;re as good as dead, and whatever foul mission the circus pursues will be that much closer to fruition. You summon your strength and courage for the long night ahead.</p><ul><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario II: The Primrose Path</b>.</li></ul>"}}},Ge={oneNightOnly:W},qe=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:Ge,oneNightOnly:W},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),Y={intro:{title:"Scenario II: The Primrose Path",body:`<p>Stories have long been told and retold in Arkham about the strange and mystical things lurking in it. Witches, demons, humanoid beasts, the list goes on. Any one of those would be reason to not venture into the woods at night, but since you're already chancing things with the circus and its monsters, there's not much left to hold you back.</p><p>The full moon lends an eerie brightness to the woods. The same atmosphere of illusory magic that you saw on the circus grounds lingers between the trees. No doubt the circus has taken precautions to veil themselves from prying outsiders, and you wonder how they and the moon align. Until then, you must decide how you will proceed into this mystical forest.</p><ul><li>The investigators must decide (choose one):<ul><li>"We'll use the moonlight to our advantage." If there is a {'{'}tablet{'}'} token in the chaos bag, remove it and add a {'{'}cultist{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>"We'll stick the shadows as much as possible." If there is a {'{'}cultist{'}'} token in the chaos bag, remove it and add a {'{'}tablet{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li></ul></li></ul>`,label:{useMoonlight:`"We'll use the moonlight to our advantage."`,shadows:`"We'll stick the shadows as much as possible."`}},bloodMoon:{label:{physicalTrauma:"Suffer 1 physical trauma",mentalTrauma:"Suffer 1 mental trauma"}},resolutions:{resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> Battered and dazed, you stumble through the ensorcelled woods, instinctive motivation for survival alone pushing you forward. Minutes pass &ndash; or are they hours? &ndash; until a much softer crunch rouses your senses. One of the circus carnies wanders by you, seemingly on patrol. The carnie must be on his way back to the camp, and if he can bypass the illusory defenses, then perhaps you can as well. You follow the man at a distance, and gradually, you tail him to the outskirts of the circus encampment.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the investigators were lost in the Arkham woods</i>.</li><li>Skip to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> Despite the fearsome challenges in the forest, you find the camp to be surprisingly placid. The performers sleep in tents or in hammocks out in the open, with only a small night guard on duty patrolling. For all the magic and monstrosity at their command, the circus is still crewed by mortal humans with common needs.</p><p>Some creatures that you faced in the woods did not even look as disguised as circus animals. They were almost formless amalgamations of mouths, tentacles, hooves and horns, scattered over a fleshy trunk like the patches on an old coat. You shudder to imagine what worse things could be at the circus' beck and call.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the investigators bypassed the illusions</i>.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"Resolution 3",body:'<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> With cautious steps, you traverse the outskirts of the circus encampment, looking for any sign of the kidnapped citizens. You reach a towering oak at the far side, ancient, twisted, and all but barren. An ornate painted trailer stands against it, larger than any of the other nearby carts by far.</p><p>The towering figure of the ringmaster emerges and descends the short steps. "Get your sleep," he utters, "the perimeter guard will let us know when they arrive." With the ringmaster out in the woods, you have a rare chance to delve into the heart of the matter. Steeling your nerve, you creep up the steps to his trailer.</p><ul><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Interlude: The Future and the Past</b>.</li></ul>'}}},Ke={thePrimrosePath:Y},Ve=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:Ke,thePrimrosePath:Y},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),O="亡者马戏团",B="<h1>新月阴影下</h1><p>新月马戏团仅在阿卡姆演出一夜，而失踪案与离奇死亡一路随团沿海蔓延。《亡者马戏团》是 Tyler Gotch 为《诡镇奇谈：卡牌版》设计的八场爱好者剧本。</p>",N={title:"附加规则：{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记",moonTokens:"<p class='basic'>本剧本引入新的混乱标记：月亮 ({'{'}moon{'}'}) 标记。在《亡者马戏团》中，月亮影响重大；{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记代表其诡异影响的强度与严重程度。</p><ul><li>技能检定中揭示{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记时：“0。将此标记封印在你的调查员卡上，再揭示一个标记。”</li><li>封印在调查员卡上的{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记本身没有效果，但部分卡牌会参照是否有{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记被封印，或封印的数量。</li><li>每轮结束时，你调查员卡上每有一个{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记，必须选择：<ul><li>该标记继续封印于调查员卡上。</li><li>承受1点伤害或1点恐惧，然后释放该标记。</li></ul></li><li>技能检定外揭示的{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记本身没有效果，除非卡牌另有说明。</li></ul>"},L={title:"序幕",body:"<p class='center'><b>****** 即将登场：新月马戏团！ ******</b></p><p class='center'><b>快来欣赏世界上最精彩的演出！</b></p><p class='center'><b>惊险杂技、无上力量与技艺、活着的不可思议生物！</b></p><p class='center'><b>本周日来到你的城镇，仅演一夜！</b></p><p class='center'><b>** 切勿错过此生仅有的机会！ **</b></p><p><i>1923年8月26日，星期日，马萨诸塞州阿卡姆。</i></p><p>新月马戏团近一周来一直是全城话题。巡回马戏团通常只为利润拜访大城市，阿卡姆人也很少有余裕随兴去波士顿、纽约或费城。就连法兰西山的上流人士都开玩笑说想去看一眼。你也对马戏团感兴趣，却不是出于那些寻常理由。</p>",minnie:"<p>《阿卡姆广告报》的明妮·克莱因最先让你注意到这些巧合。你在维尔玛小餐馆找到明妮时，她手里拿着记事本，眼中透着一股饥渴，而且显然不是冲着午餐特餐来的。“看看这个。”她说着把铅笔当作老师的教鞭，指向本上的记录，“新月马戏团以前都在南方走常规巡演路线，亚特兰大、杰克逊维尔这类大城市一站不落，最北也从没越过孟菲斯。可一个月前，他们突然沿海岸北上，一路专挑偏僻小镇演出。阿卡姆是他们离开萨凡纳后到过的最大城镇。”</p><p>你承认马戏团改变路线的背后多半有些古怪，却仍不明白明妮为何如此兴奋。她立刻解释：“新月马戏团到过的每一座城镇，都在他们停留期间发生了失踪案和离奇死亡。更要紧的是这个。”明妮得意地笑着，用手指点了点记事本底部，“去看过马戏团的人，没一个记得演出的具体内容。两个住在相隔三个州的人，向各自当地报纸描述经历时，居然说了完全相同的话。这还不够可疑吗？”</p><p>至少可疑到了值得你调查一番的程度。于是，你备好门票，也为一切可能的意外作足准备，动身前往马戏团。由于时节尚早，傍晚依旧明亮，但一轮满月已经升上天空。</p>",addMoonTokens:"将3个 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记加入混乱袋，直到剧本结束。"},H={label:{endOfRoundQuestion:"你的调查员卡上封印了一个 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记。你必须选择一项：",keepSealed:"该标记继续封印在你的调查员卡上",takeDamageAndRelease:"承受1点伤害，然后释放该标记",takeHorrorAndRelease:"承受1点恐惧，然后释放该标记"}},j={doneReleasingMoonTokens:"{'{'}moon{'}'} 标记释放完毕"},F={cluesToSpend:"要花费的线索"},z={theRingmasterDoesNotSuspectYou:"团长没有怀疑你。",theRingmasterHasHisEyeOnYou:"团长盯上你了。",theInvestigatorsWereLostInTheArkhamWoods:"调查员迷失在阿卡姆树林中。",theInvestigatorsBypassedTheIllusions:"调查员绕过了幻象。",groupsOfCitizensWereSavedFromTheCircus:"从马戏团救出的市民群体",theRingmasterHadDaysToPrepare:"团长获得的准备天数",theInvestigatorsCouldNotEscapeTheCircus:"调查员未能逃离马戏团。",theInvestigatorsClashedWithBlake:"调查员与布莱克交锋。",theInvestigatorsUnmaskedBlake:"调查员揭露了布莱克。",theInvestigatorsStruckDownBlake:"调查员击倒了布莱克。",theInvestigatorsMustFollowTheCult:"调查员必须追随邪教。",theInvestigatorsDiscoveredTheRitualsLocation:"调查员发现了仪式地点。",theInvestigatorsDidNotArriveInTime:"调查员未能及时抵达。",theCultRallies:"邪教集结。",theInvestigatorsWereDevouredByTheThousandYoung:"调查员被千仔吞噬。",theInvestigatorsEndedTheRitual:"调查员终止了仪式。",shubNiggurathReignsOverAnEclipsedWorld:"莎布·尼古拉丝统治着日蚀世界。",shubNiggurathVanishedWithTheEclipse:"莎布·尼古拉丝随日蚀消失。",theProphecyWasFulfilled:"预言实现了。",theProphecyWasUnfulfilled:"预言未能实现。",destinies:"命运",theNewMoonCircusWasNeverSeenAgain:"新月马戏团从此销声匿迹。",theNewMoonCircusMaySomedayReturn:"新月马戏团也许终会归来。"},Xe={name:O,intro:B,additionalRules:N,prologue:L,moonToken:H,label:j,illusoryLocus:F,key:z},$e=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,additionalRules:N,default:Xe,illusoryLocus:F,intro:B,key:z,label:j,moonToken:H,name:O,prologue:L},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),G={title:"幕间：未来与过去",intro:"<p>谢天谢地，团长拖车的门开合时几乎没有一点声音。车内陈设奢华，每件家具和装饰都用上乘材料制成。一面书架摆满秘学典籍，光是书脊上的文字便令你心生不安。你才刚开始翻找，一阵轻响便将你的注意力引向把拖车隔成两半的深色帘幕。你小心做好应付麻烦的准备，一把掀开帘子。</p><p>后半部同样富丽堂皇，但你根本无暇留意。一位身着占卜师服饰的深肤色女子被绑在椅子上，嘴也被堵住，精疲力竭地微微动弹。她抬起疲惫的双眼望向你，转眼间又因震惊而睁大。你伸手去解她嘴后的布结，女子身子前倾，呼吸越来越急促。“是你！”她压低声音喘道。嗓音虽干涩，仍带着柔和的南方口音，“我在异象里见过你！这一切……真的发生了！”</p>",farSeeing:{title:"远见",body:"<p><i>若本剧本选择了1位或更多通灵调查员，则这些调查员阅读“远见”。</i></p><p>你对未来的一瞥并不陌生，但你更习惯看见别人，而不是被别人看见。得知自己也在这名女子的异象中扮演某种角色，让你对自己的能力有了新的认识。</p><p class='basic'>你获得1点奖励经验值，这点经验只能用于购买<i>预兆</i>卡牌。</p>"},xp:{farSeeing:"远见"},thea:"<p>回想起之前的遭遇，西娅打了个寒颤。“他强迫我说出异象。不是用蛮力，而是对我的心智……他用魔法像榨橙子一样挤压我的脑袋，逼我说出那些连自己都不知道的事情……我拼尽全力，才没有透露谁能阻止他的具体细节……只告诉他你们在阿卡姆。这是我唯一的希望……见到你们真是太好了。”</p><p>一时间，你很难消化这一切。无论你是否相信西娅的话，布莱克确实为了追捕预见他失败的人，把马戏团一路带到了北方的阿卡姆。你们试图阻止他大开杀戒，他尤其不会放过你们。你问西娅，布莱克究竟想阻止你们插手什么事。她恍惚地点点头。“我也不完全清楚，但我给你看一样东西。我相信我们能一起弄明白。”</p>",addAmaltheaWeaver:"一位调查员必须将阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（马戏团占卜师）加入其牌组。此卡不计入该调查员的牌组张数。",theTome:"<p>西娅渐渐恢复了力气，指引你回到拖车前半部的秘学书架。“那一本，浅棕色皮封面的。”她示意道。你从书架上抽出饱经风霜的古书，端详它的封面。封面饰有怪异符号，但除此之外与旁边的典籍并无区别。你解开搭扣，查看里面泛黄的羊皮纸。</p>",linguaFranca:{title:"通用语言",body:"<p><i>若本剧本选择了1位或更多米斯卡塔尼克、学者或信徒调查员，则这些调查员阅读“通用语言”。</i></p><p>尽管年代久远，书中字迹依然清晰，所用词句也能辨认。由于成长经历，你对拉丁文颇为熟悉，读起来毫不费力。若这本古书确实重要，接下来的任务至少简单了一些。</p><p class='basic'>你在下场冒险的起始手牌中多抽取1张卡牌。</p>"},apuleius:"<p>你研究古书的第一页时，西娅站在一旁。“原来就是这本。布莱克审问我时，经常把它拿在手里。”她的手指划过页首的一个词。“阿普列乌斯。”她低声念道。你问西娅能读懂多少。“大部分都行。以前马戏团里有位魔术师教过我拉丁文读写，说这样能让我的占卜表演更有味道。如今想来，仿佛已经过了很久……”你合上古书，把它收进随身物品。以后还有时间研究其中的秘密，现在必须先逃出布莱克的掌控。</p>",addDeCultusBestiae:"一位调查员必须将《兽类崇拜》（阿普列乌斯遗作）加入其牌组。此卡不计入该调查员的牌组张数。",eclipse:"<p>你随口问起这本古书与西娅的异象有何关联。西娅绞着双手回答：“异象里还有一件事，我总能看见……日蚀。一次日全蚀。”</p>",likeClockwork:{title:"如同钟表",body:"<p><i>若本剧本选择了诺曼·威瑟斯，则该调查员阅读“如同钟表”。</i></p><p>天文学界早已有了预测日月运行的模型。虽然你更擅长研究星辰，这个话题仍唤起了一些被你搁置已久的学术记忆。</p><p class='basic'>你的牌组构筑选项获得“至多额外2张等级1-2的探求者卡牌（&loz;）”。</p>"},escape:"<p>日全蚀。这一天象本身便充满神秘色彩，但它对西尔维斯特·布莱克及其马戏团究竟有何意义，依然不得而知。答案一定藏在那本皮革装订的古书中，可你现在没时间留在这里研究。你让西娅等大家安全离开营地，并尽可能救出被囚的平民后，再仔细回想她的异象。她答应下来，准备谨慎地争取自由。此时此刻，你只希望满月能暂时消失，好为逃亡提供掩护。</p>",addMoonToken:"将1个 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记加入混乱袋，直到剧本结束。"},q={title:"幕间：石中所书",intro:"<p>有人敲响你的房门，顿时驱散了脑中的倦意。你小心开门，发现门外是西娅，她的房间就在走廊对面，怀里紧抱着那本古书。你连忙请她进来，锁上房门。“路上一直没有机会，但我必须告诉你们，我从这本书里发现了什么。”</p><p>“这本《兽类崇拜》出自生活在罗马帝国时期的阿普列乌斯。他既是学者，也是诗人，还涉足过好几个教派。通常来说，那些教派只是崇拜罗马万神殿中的特定神祇，但这份记载讲的却是……莎布·尼古拉丝的教派。”</p><p>书中详细记述了一个伪装成巴克科斯教派的莎布·尼古拉丝教团，以及阿普列乌斯如何潜入其中、获悉其秘密，又怎样协助当地的罗马总督瓦解了那个地区的教团。你们最近已经亲身见识过书中大部分恐怖事物，但西娅接下来讲出的几项关键发现仍令你心惊。</p><p>“他声称，在任意一个新月之夜，都能于森林中用仪式召唤莎布·尼古拉丝，但祂只能短暂停留。当年的教团正在设计一场仪式，想在日蚀期间锁住月亮，让他们的神永久降临；不过教团被驱散时，所有研究成果都被焚毁了。大祭司在受刑前宣告了一则预言，阿普列乌斯把它记录在这本书里。”</p><p>西娅指给你看其中一段，一边阅读一边翻译：“凭森林之主、母神配偶的狡智，失落之言将重为世人所知，祂强大的幼子将得喂养，黑色天幕的群星将列位齐整。待月日再无光芒，黎明与森林皆染猩红。伊阿！莎布·尼古拉丝！森之黑山羊，孕育千万子孙之母！”</p>",prophecy:"<p>念完这段文字，西娅干涩地咽了口唾沫。“现在我能体会他的心情了。这则预言后面紧接着一小段向狄安娜祈求保护的祷文。她是罗马的野兽、狩猎与月亮女神。”她再次把书指给你看，这次直接念出了那句拉丁文。</p>",addInvocationOfDiana:"每位调查员可以将一张“狄安娜的祈唤”加入其牌组。这些卡不计入这些调查员的牌组张数。",role:"<p>西娅读出预言中那些人物的描述，你不得不承认，你们确实很符合。你当然无法确定近两千年前的女祭司是否真能清楚看见你们，但这并不比过去两周发生的其他离奇事件更不可思议。西娅看看你们，又看看书中文字，神情渐渐变得不安。“你们明明白白地写在这里，可是……我只想知道，我自己接下来还要做什么。如果这一切都是真的，那些异象只是为了把你们卷进来，而现在……我的使命就到此为止了吗？”</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",determination:"<p><b>决心：</b>你认为预言只不过是从时间的钥匙孔窥视未来。西娅没有出现在那一小片可见景象中，并不意味着她不在场，更不意味着她没有发挥关键作用。“比如说，预言里哪里提到过他们？可正是他们把你带到这里。”西娅长长吐出一口气，明显放松下来。“你们说得对。我得把事情掌握在自己手里，相信自己的所作所为确实有意义。你们甚至在知道预言以前，就已经这么做了。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（勇气追寻者）。</p>",guidance:"<p><b>指引：</b>你认为她的异象或许是同一则预言的延伸。古代女祭司能看见和理解的毕竟有限，也许应由西娅补完其余内容。说到底，正是她的能力与知识让你们读懂了这则古老预言。西娅低头看着手里的书，默默点头。“你们说得对。我不能再用这么狭窄的眼光看待异象。里面一定还有更多内容，只要我能专心弄懂它们。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（智慧追寻者）。</p>",furtherReading:{title:"进一步阅读",body:"<p>西娅翻回写着亵渎宣言的那一页，皱眉沉思。“我只希望我们知道布莱克究竟在谋划什么。他似乎已经集齐这则预言所需的一切，也只需要来加利福尼亚等候日蚀，那为什么还要特地追杀你们？他对这些预言和自己的异象深信不疑，可究竟是为什么？”</p>"},noChoice:{title:"别无选择",body:"<p><i>若本剧本选择了1位或更多天选调查员，则阅读“别无选择”。</i></p><p>你无法理解布莱克那般扭曲邪恶的心智，但你早已接受自己在这些事件中的位置，因此多少能洞察他的执念。</p><p class='basic'>你可以治疗1点肉体或精神创伤。</p>"},motive:"<p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",fanaticism:"<p><b>狂热：</b>你提出，既然布莱克侍奉莎布·尼古拉丝，这场仪式便已酝酿千年。他宁死也不愿教团再次失败，因此必会逐字逐句照着阿普列乌斯的古书完成任务。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（信念诠释）。</p>",nemesis:"<p><b>宿敌：</b>你提出，对布莱克这样自信而准备周全的人来说，你们出现在预言里绝不只是几句文字。你们偷走阿普列乌斯古书的举动，很可能也让此事成了私人恩怨，进一步点燃了他对你们原有的仇恨。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（执念诠释）。</p>",bookmark:"<p><b>书签：</b>关于预言与布莱克，你们还能提出无数理论。眼下的推测只是暂时停下的一页，必须在行动中找出答案。</p>",addSkullToken:"将1个 {'{'}skull{'}'} 标记加入混乱袋，直到剧本结束。",label:{addInvocationOfDianaQuestion:"你可以将一张“狄安娜的祈唤”加入牌组；它不计入牌组张数。",addInvocationOfDiana:"将“狄安娜的祈唤”加入牌组",doNotAddInvocationOfDiana:"不加入“狄安娜的祈唤”",determination:"“预言只有在像你们这样的人采取行动时才会发生。”",guidance:"“你或许与狄安娜女祭司承担着相似角色。”",healTraumaQuestion:"别无选择：你可以治疗1点肉体或精神创伤。",healPhysicalTrauma:"治疗1点肉体创伤",healMentalTrauma:"治疗1点精神创伤",doNotHealTrauma:"不治疗创伤",fanaticism:"“也许他狂热到除此之外什么都不在乎。”",nemesis:"“也许在他看来，我们就是他个人失败的象征。”"}},K={title:"幕间：吉兆",intro:"<p>你们踏上北行之路时，第一缕阳光开始温暖整座城市。西娅全神贯注地研读阿普列乌斯记载的最后一页，嘴唇默念着拉丁文，在每个词上都反复琢磨。良久，她终于转向你……</p>",moreToDo:"<p><b>尚有可为：</b>“我一直在尝试更直接地控制异象。确实有些效果，但是……异象实在太多了。想把它们全部看清，就会漏掉其中的细节。换作你们，会怎样判断哪些异象最重要？”</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",priorWarning:"<p><b>预先警告：</b>西娅点点头，安详地微笑着合上书。“我就照你们说的做。虽然本该是我为你们指引方向，你们却已经给了我许多指引。不过现在肯定轮到我了。不管他们想出什么花招，我们都会有所准备。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（纯洁神谕者）。</p>",sawItComing:"<p><b>早有预见：</b>西娅点点头，勇敢地微笑着合上书。“我就照你们说的做。虽然本该是我为你们指引方向，你们却已经给了我许多指引。不过现在肯定轮到我了。他们的一举一动都逃不过我们的眼睛。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（坚毅神谕者）。</p>",moreToSee:"<p><b>尚有可见：</b>“我一直在试着更彻底地向异象敞开心扉，让它们完整上演，揭示我先前未曾看见的事情。只是……我不知道该怎样解读。换作你们，会如何看待这些异象与预言？”</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",writtenInInk:"<p><b>墨中所书：</b>西娅回头望向古书。“我就照你们说的做。虽然本该是我为你们指引方向，你们却已经给了我许多指引。不过现在肯定轮到我了。我们要确保这则预言完全按计划发展。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（启迪神谕者）。</p>",writtenInSmoke:"<p><b>烟中所书：</b>西娅回头望向古书。“我就照你们说的做。虽然本该是我为你们指引方向，你们却已经给了我许多指引。不过现在肯定轮到我了。我们要确保命运掌握在自己手中。”</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员将其替换为阿玛尔西娅·韦弗（神秘神谕者）。</p>",theLastWord:{title:"最后一句话",body:"<p>你也想起那本古书，纳闷邪教究竟知道了什么。书曾在布莱克手中，或许他留下的每一句话都在为你们指向终局。</p>"},theInfinite:"<p><b>无限：</b>如果你们判断正确，布莱克的动力确实来自虔诚信仰，他的追随者就会把主要精力投入仪式，依靠那邪恶咒法带领他们取胜。</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",powersAbove:"<p><b>上方之力：</b>从某种意义上说，是这本古书一路指引你们来到这里，现在没有理由偏离这条道路。此时此刻，你们比以往任何时候都更需要书中的咒文。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（彼界预言）。</p>",powersBelow:"<p><b>下方之力：</b>从某种意义上说，是这本古书一路指引你们来到这里，但若没有你们自己的本领，它也无法走到这么远。今天早晨，谨慎运用此书才是最明智的做法。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（永恒预言）。</p>",theEndless:"<p><b>无尽：</b>如果你们判断正确，布莱克的动力确实来自复仇，他的追随者就会依靠他们神祇的实体眷属，借助羊魔与邪恶黑山羊幼崽取得胜利。</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须决定（选择一项）：</p>",againstTheFlood:"<p><b>逆潮：</b>古书将莎布·尼古拉丝称为“孕育千万子孙的森之黑山羊”，你们必须做好准备，在今天结束以前迎战并击败无数敌人。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（群军预言）。</p>",againstTheStorm:"<p><b>逆风暴：</b>你们已经无数次见识过莎布·尼古拉丝最强大子嗣那惊人的体型与力量。今天，你们必须竭尽所能与它们抗衡。</p><p class='basic'>牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员将其替换为《兽类崇拜》（巨兽预言）。</p>",breakOfDawn:"<p><b>破晓：</b>晨光渐亮，你和西娅一边向洛杉矶北方前行，一边疲惫地低声交谈。澄澈的天空丝毫未能缓解你们对即将到来之战的忧虑。</p>",addSkullToken:"将1个 {'{'}skull{'}'} 标记加入混乱袋，直到剧本结束。",label:{priorWarning:"“专注用异象保护我们。”",sawItComing:"“专注用异象对抗怪物。”",writtenInInk:"“让异象与文本预言相互印证。”",writtenInSmoke:"“接受异象本来的样子，超越预言。”",powersAbove:"“我们必须依靠超越人类的力量指引。”",powersBelow:"“这场战斗必须依靠我们自身的力量。”",againstTheFlood:"“我们必须准备面对千军万马。”",againstTheStorm:"“我们必须准备面对巨物。”"}},V={title:"尾声",intro:"<p><i>仅当调查员赢得剧本时阅读以下内容。</i></p><p>想到自由父亲协会也许正在洛杉矶等候报复，你们没有原路折返，而是离开红杉林，向北前往旧金山。这段可怕经历让你们对一切森林都心生戒备，眼下只盼乘火车穿越开阔平原，返回故乡。</p>",underWraps:{title:"包裹严实",body:"<p><i>若某调查员牌组中有“兽性变化”，该调查员阅读“包裹严实”。</i></p><p>日蚀下的大战结束后，那些野蛮冲动大多平息了，但你知道自己必须时刻与之抗争，甚至可能持续余生。在找到解除鲁加鲁诅咒的方法以前，总得有人流血，无论以哪种方式。</p>"},divergingPaths:{title:"分岔路径",body:"<p><i>若某调查员牌组中有埃斯普利女士，该调查员阅读“分岔路径”。</i></p><p>红杉林中的苦难结束后，埃斯普利女士一直比平常更加疏离。旅途再次来到圣路易斯时，你登上前往芝加哥的火车，那位巫毒祭司却留在站台上。“勒格巴老爹站在十字路口，会指引我前往最需要我的地方。不过别担心。你若需要我，条条道路终会再次把我带到你身边。”</p>"},thea:"<p>返回阿卡姆的路上，西娅始终陪在你们身边，只是少言寡语。自布莱克掌控四叶草马戏团以来，她的人生便被一路推向那场日蚀仪式。所有事情都为那一刻层层累积，而如今仪式已经结束，她反而无所适从。就连西娅的异象，也没有显现任何明确的未来。打个比方，她的未来如今是一页白纸，尽管她仍把《兽类崇拜》牢牢握在手边。</p>",kernelOfTruth:{title:"真相之核",body:"<p><i>若预言实现：</i></p><p>西娅用手轻抚古书饱经风霜的封面。“想到那些古人竟如此信任我们，实在奇怪。女祭司和阿普列乌斯都不知道教团到底在做什么，也不知道该怎样阻止他们，只能……寄予希望。我想，至少我也懂得这种希望。”</p><p class='basic'>每位调查员获得2点奖励经验值，因为他们理解了自己在那些超越真正认知的事件中所扮演的角色。</p>"},xp:{kernelOfTruth:"真相之核"},grainOfSalt:{title:"一粒盐",body:"<p><i>若预言未实现：</i></p><p>西娅双手捧着古书，仿佛凝视一块墓碑。“我不知道女祭司究竟看见了什么，又漏掉了什么，但这则预言已经完成了它的使命。就算那些华丽词句唯一的作用只是把你们引到那片森林，哪些是真相、哪些只是希望也已经不重要了。女祭司只是希望未来不会落入教团手中，我无法因此责怪她。”</p>"},lookingAhead:{title:"展望前方",body:"<p>你们合上了人生中这段近乎字面意义上的篇章，可未来的问题依然存在。你问西娅，如果一路随你们回到阿卡姆，她以后打算怎么办。“我还没想明白。经历了这一切，我想自己不可能再回马戏团生活了。往后若还能看见哪怕只有这次一半重要的异象，它们的价值也远不止一张马戏票。不过在那以前，我总得先养活自己。”</p><p>你提议把西娅介绍给阿卡姆的一些盟友，例如亨利·阿米蒂奇博士。她精通拉丁文，又拥有远超常人所愿承受的秘学经历，必会成为米斯卡塔尼克图书馆的宝贵助力。占卜师望向车窗，带着惆怅的神情凝视飞驰而过的景色。“不试试怎么知道，对吧？”</p><p>你们回到阿卡姆时，几乎没有引起任何关注。市民一心想在这座城市里找回些许正常生活，马戏团的事情大多已被遗忘。拉尔夫与凯莉·戴克斯特拉在北区站台看见你们，兴高采烈地上前重逢并道贺。明妮·克莱因很快也赶来，急着收获自己种下的新闻线索。她很清楚编辑多伊尔·杰弗里斯绝不会刊登半个字，但至少满足了自己的好奇心。对你们而言，这两场短暂会面意义非凡；可对不知内情的旁人来说，根本不值得多看一眼。</p><p>西娅带着满心感激一一道别，前往南区，在找到新去处以前暂住于妈妈的寄宿屋。近一个月来，你终于第一次独自一人。</p>"},restAssured:{title:"安心休息",body:"<p>你沿着河岸城熟悉的道路走回家，在九月凉爽的空气里享受片刻喘息。即使天气晴好，阿卡姆依然阴沉，正适合无数隐秘而阴险的邪恶潜伏。相比之下，你几乎庆幸这次的邪恶像有毒爬虫般招摇现身。若这场阴谋从头到尾都藏在暗处，恐怕根本没有机会揭开真相。此事提醒你必须时刻警惕，绝不可只看事物表面。马戏团有句老话：每分钟都有一个傻瓜诞生。</p><p class='basic'>在你的剧本日志中，记录<i>新月马戏团从此销声匿迹</i>。</p>"},encore:{title:"加演曲目",body:"<p>你沿着河岸城熟悉的道路走回家，在九月凉爽的空气里享受片刻喘息。这让你有时间回想过去发生的一切，尤其是西尔维斯特·布莱克。尽管你们在森林中获胜，布莱克却消失得无影无踪。你确信自己还会再见到他。团长既记仇又狡猾，只要他还有一丝卷土重来的可能，你就必须提防背后。下次他或许还会打着新月马戏团的幌子，也或许不会，因为邪恶有着无数张面孔。</p><p class='basic'>在你的剧本日志中，记录<i>新月马戏团也许终会归来</i>。牌组中有阿玛尔西娅·韦弗的调查员必须将1张“高塔·XVI”加入其牌组。牌组中有《兽类崇拜》的调查员必须将1张“恶魔·XV”加入其牌组。</p>"}},Ue={theFutureAndThePast:G,writtenInStone:q,goodOmens:K,epilogue:V},Qe=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:Ue,epilogue:V,goodOmens:K,theFutureAndThePast:G,writtenInStone:q},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),X={intro:{title:"冒险I：仅此一夜",body:"<p>你走近马戏团场地时，住宅区南面的树林在渐暗天光中耸立于眼前。笑容满面的招徕人收下门票，一边领你入场，一边热情高喊着各种精彩节目，但你只留意其中潜藏的威胁。若这座马戏团真藏着黑暗致命之物，你便一刻也不能放松警惕。你随着人流走向主帐篷，心中猜测麻烦会从何处开始。</p><p>一阵嘹亮的号声骤然响起，珍奇异兽与盛装杂技演员组成的长队蜿蜒穿过帐篷，在观众的掌声中各自进入表演场。一名高得异乎寻常的男子留着尖胡子、身穿漆黑礼服，悠然走过三座表演场，向观众优雅鞠躬。他抬起头，准备向欢呼的市民致辞时，你从他眼中捕捉到一丝令人不安的光芒。</p><p><i>“女士们、先生们，男孩们、女孩们，欢迎观赏你们此生最伟大的奇观！看好了，我，西尔维斯特·布莱克，新月马戏团的团长，即将揭晓我们最不可思议的戏法！”</i>团长的声音响彻帐篷，语调却和他的外表一样不自然。他以魔术师般灵巧的动作挥舞双手，一头大象随即昂身长鸣。观众席爆发出欢呼与掌声，大象再次做出相同动作，可叫声开始扭曲，身形也随之摇曳。当它第三次昂起身体时，头颅竟从中裂开，发出的嘶鸣全然不似尘世之声。人群的欢呼化作惊恐尖叫，整座帐篷顿时陷入混乱。</p>",behindTheCurtain:"<p><b>帷幕后方：</b><i>你在露天看台落座时，目光本能地飘向演员们上场前聚集的地方。少数露面的成员鬼祟地扫视四周，练习着古怪的手势。</i></p><p>你从标记池获得1个线索，并带着它开始游戏。</p>"},seats:{label:{firstRing:"“我要坐在动物表演旁边。”你从大帐篷（第一表演场）开始游戏。",secondRing:"“我要坐在杂技演员旁边。”你从大帐篷（第二表演场）开始游戏。",thirdRing:"“我要坐在小丑旁边。”你从大帐篷（第三表演场）开始游戏。"}},houseOfHorrors:{label:{discardHalfHand:"弃掉你一半的手牌（向上取整）",sealMoonToken:"从混乱袋中查找一个 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记，并将其封印在你的调查员卡上"}},mesmericMagic:{label:{physicalTrauma:"承受1点肉体创伤",mentalTrauma:"承受1点精神创伤"}},resolutions:{resolution1:{title:"结局1",body:"<p>身下地面的粗糙摩擦与林间夜行动物的声响，让你缓慢却确实地恢复了意识。你昏昏沉沉地睁开一只眼，发现一名马戏团杂役正拖着你穿过树林，继续向阿卡姆南方走去。虽然后脑为此挨出一个肿包，但你总算离开了那座受诅咒的马戏团，也摆脱了幻象的影响。</p><p>你鼓起力气，胡乱一拳击中绑架者的肾部。他痛呼一声，把你摔在地上。你迅速撑起身体，准备在必要时为自由一战。那杂役上下打量着你，同样作好再次交手的准备，却忽然抬头望向你们上方的满月。他面露苦色，转身以惊人速度朝树林深处狂奔，身手远比外表看起来敏捷。阿卡姆树林地势险恶，你多半追不上他，但至少知道他眼下另有更要紧的事。</p><ul><li>在剧本日志中记录：<i>团长没有怀疑你</i>。</li><li>若游戏结束时为场景1，查看本场冒险所选场景1的背面，并将其列出的标记加入混乱袋，直到战役结束。</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"结局2",body:"<p>你快步踏上通往马戏团的干燥土路，数十名惊魂未定的幸存者紧随其后。暂时远离屠杀与绑架后，你劝众人尽快返回阿卡姆并通知警方。阿卡姆的警察虽不怎么可靠，但马戏团的戏法再高明，也掩盖不了今晚发生的一切。</p><p>受害者陆续返回安全之地，你的思绪却又转向身后那座依旧高耸的马戏团。他们究竟为何这么做？能操纵那些可怖野兽、施展催眠魔法的人，不会只因纯粹的恶意便组织这一切。再想到明妮报告中那场突然北上的巡演，今晚的混乱背后必然有某种明确目的。可那目的究竟是什么？</p><p>团长西尔维斯特·布莱克一定知道全部答案。他外表如此醒目而危险，照理不难追踪，却在混乱开始后不久便消失无踪，恐怕又是马戏团的幻术。他是不愿亲自动手，还是另有理由刻意置身事外？终有一天真相会浮出水面，因为你还打算当面向他问个明白。</p><ul><li>在剧本日志中记录：<i>团长盯上你了</i>。</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"结局3",body:"<p>附近一声尖叫再次令你精神一振，你冲进林线。一名面容瘦削、棱角分明的马戏团演员紧抓着一个小男孩，正试图将他拖往树林深处。你靠近时踩断一根细枝，绑架者猛地抬头看了你一眼，随即抛下猎物逃进森林。男孩手脚并用地退到一棵树旁，直到你平静地自我介绍，他才明显安定下来。你让他立刻返回阿卡姆。他含糊地道了声谢，转身飞奔而去。</p><p>救下一个，还有几十个。你再次望向月光下的树林。阿卡姆人连白天都大多避开这里，更不用说危机四伏的夜晚，可你别无选择。混乱中，马戏团演员一定绑走了几十人。若不能赶在马戏团离开前于今晚救出受害者，他们便必死无疑，而马戏团追求的邪恶使命也会离实现更近一步。你为前方漫漫长夜鼓起力量与勇气。</p><ul><li>每位调查员获得经验值，数量等同于胜利区中所有卡牌的胜利X数值之和。</li></ul>"}}},Je={oneNightOnly:X},Ze=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:Je,oneNightOnly:X},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),$={intro:{title:"冒险II：樱草花径",body:"<p>阿卡姆长久流传着树林中潜伏诡异神秘之物的故事：女巫、恶魔、类人生兽，数不胜数。它们本足以让人不在夜里踏进树林，但既然你已冒险追查马戏团和它的怪物，也没有多少东西能再拦住你。</p><p>满月给树林投下不祥的明亮光芒。你在马戏团地面见过的幻术气息仍缠绕树间；马戏团显然用它屏蔽外人的窥探。你必须决定如何进入这片魔法森林。</p>",label:{useMoonlight:"“我们利用月光。”若混乱袋中有 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记，移除它，并加入1个 {'{'}tablet{'}'} 标记，直到剧本结束。",shadows:"“尽量待在阴影里。”若混乱袋中有 {'{'}tablet{'}'} 标记，移除它，并加入1个 {'{'}moon{'}'} 标记，直到剧本结束。"}},bloodMoon:{label:{physicalTrauma:"承受1点肉体创伤",mentalTrauma:"承受1点精神创伤"}},resolutions:{resolution1:{title:"结局1",body:"<p>你遍体鳞伤、头昏脑涨地穿过施法的树林，仅凭求生本能向前。过了不知几分钟还是几小时，一阵轻微脚步声使你清醒：一名马戏团杂役似乎在巡逻。他若能穿过幻术防线，你也许也能。你远远跟着他，最终来到马戏团营地边缘。</p><p>在剧本日志中记录：<b>调查员迷失在阿卡姆树林中</b>。</p>"},resolution2:{title:"结局2",body:"<p>尽管树林危险重重，营地却意外平静。演员们睡在帐篷或露天吊床中，只有少数夜卫巡逻；不管掌握多少魔法和怪物，马戏团仍由有寻常需求的凡人组成。</p><p>你在树林遇到的某些生物甚至不像伪装成动物的怪兽，而是由嘴、触手、蹄与角杂乱拼成的无形肉团。你不愿去想还有什么更可怕的东西听从马戏团差遣。</p><p>在剧本日志中记录：<b>调查员绕过了幻象</b>。</p>"},resolution3:{title:"结局3",body:"<p>你谨慎绕行营地边缘，寻找被绑架市民的踪迹。营地尽头有一棵高耸、扭曲、近乎枯死的老橡树，旁边停着一辆华丽彩绘的拖车，比周围任何车厢都大。高大的团长走出拖车，说道：“去睡吧，外围守卫会在他们到时通知我们。”团长进入树林后，你终于有机会深入真相；鼓足勇气，你悄悄踏上他的拖车台阶。</p><p>每位调查员获得等同于胜利区每张卡胜利X值的经验值（共 {'{'}xp{'}'} 点）。</p>"}}},et={thePrimrosePath:$},tt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:et,thePrimrosePath:$},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),U="Dark Matter",Q={heirToCarcosa:"Heir to Carcosa"},J={title:"In Space, No One Can Hear You Scream",body:"<p class='basic'>“He mentioned the establishment of the Dynasty in Carcosa, the lakes which connected Hastur, Aldebaran, and the mystery of the Hyades. He spoke of Cassilda and Camilla, and sounded the cloudy depths of Demhe and the Lake of Hali.”</p><p class='basic right'>– Robert W. Chambers, “The Repairer of Reputations”</p><p>It is 2147, and you have just woken up from cryo-sleep in a seemingly abandoned space ship – and from there on you are thrown into a deep space adventure across the solar system to prevent the extinction of the human race. Based on Call of Cthulhu supplements Ripples from Carcosa by Oscar Rios and the End Time by Dr. Michael C. LaBossiere, <i>Dark Matter</i> is an 8 scenario fan-made campaign for <i>Arkham Horror: The Card Game</i> for 1–4 players, designed by Axolotl. It requires <i>The Path to Carcosa</i> deluxe expansion; for the best experience, it is highly recommended that you have completed <i>The Path to Carcosa</i> before playing.</p>"},Z=[{title:"Scan",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.scan"},{title:"Memories",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.memories"},{title:"Alert",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.alert"}],ee={title:"Additional Rules & Clarifications",scan:"<h3>Scan</h3><p class='basic'>Some encounter cards in this campaign will have icons indicated on the bottom of the card when they are face down. These encounter cards will be used to form the “scanning deck”, an out of play deck of cards that will be constructed during the setup of some scenarios.</p><p class='basic'>In this campaign, abilities identified by the <b>Scan</b> action designator allow investigators to explore your environment. Such abilities are generally used to find story assets, story cards or locations in the scanning deck to help progress within each scenario, and are usually, but not always, initiated using the “activate” action.</p><p class='basic'><b>Scan</b> abilities instruct you to search for the top card of the scanning deck matching a certain icon. In such cases, look at the icons on the bottom of the top card in the scanning deck. <b>If the top card of the scanning deck has an icon matching the icon you are scanning for, draw that card.</b> This is considered a “successful” scan. If no cards were drawn, the scan is considered to be “unsuccessful”.</p><p class='basic'>If the topmost card does not have a matching icon, place it face down next to the scanning deck, and look for a matching icon on the next card of the scanning deck. Repeat this process until a card of the indicated type is drawn. After this action has ended, shuffle each card next to the scanning deck back into the scanning deck.</p><p class='basic'><b>Scan</b> abilities will usually, but not always, refer to the icon of a location. The icon of a location is the connection symbol that is located in the top left corner of the card.</p><p class='basic'>If such a situation arises that you would need to discard a card with the scanning back or shuffle it into any other deck, shuffle it back into the scanning deck instead.</p>",memories:"<h3>Memories</h3><p class='basic'>Some scenario cards, story resolutions and interludes may refer to your “Memories”. Each investigator has a section in the Campaign Log to mark their individual “Memories”. <b>These “Memories” are tied to specific investigators, and are not shared among all of the investigators.</b></p><p class='basic'>You may be instructed to add tally marks or cross out tally marks to specific investigator’s “Memories”. This is done by marking a line in that investigator’s “Memories” section in the Campaign Log, or crossing out one of the above lines, respectively. The number of “Memories” each investigator has is equal to the number of tally marks in their respective sections that have not been crossed out.</p>",alert:"<h3>Alert</h3><p class='basic'>Each time an investigator fails a skill test while attempting to evade an enemy with the alert keyword, after applying all results for that skill test, that enemy performs an attack against the evading investigator. An enemy does not exhaust after performing an alert attack. This attack occurs whether the enemy is engaged with the evading investigator or not.</p>"},te={title:"Prologue",body:"<p>You turn over the folded program in your hand, reading it for what seems like the hundredth time. “Miskatonic Playhouse presents: The King in Yellow,” it reads. “A special one-night engagement at Arkham’s very own Ward Theatre. An irresistible drama in two acts. Production staged and directed by Nigel Engram.” The cast is a small ensemble, with one unattributed credit at the end: “The Stranger.”</p><p>To have such a highly anticipated play come to Arkham all the way from Paris is a noteworthy event, even if it is just for one night. For weeks leading up to the show, it was the talk of the town. It seemed so unassuming… and yet, you have evidence something sinister is at work. It started with the disappearance of one of the stagehands at the theatre—a boy of only seventeen who missed rehearsal one night and was never seen again. Then, less than two weeks before the performance, there was the musician whose corpse was found with a gun in its mouth. Perhaps most chilling was the crazed man the coppers had picked up in Independence Square who had been ranting and raving about the “King’s return.” He was brought to Arkham Asylum, and you were surprised to discover that he was not alone in his delusions.</p><p>Finding these events suspicious, you and your companions have delved deeper into the matter. Although no connection can be proven, these weren’t the only strange events surrounding the up-and-coming play. Instances of suicide and madness have followed in its wake, and you are determined to discover why.</p><p>The lights in the auditorium dim, and a spotlight shines on the stage. What unfolds is not quite what you expected. Slow-paced and monotonous, the first act of <i>The King in Yellow</i> is a tedious bore. The setting and characters are compelling, but the meandering and nonsensical story does little to entertain or inform. You begin to wonder whether the dreadful events surrounding <i>The King in Yellow</i> aren’t connected, after all. Perhaps it was just your overactive imagination; how could such a trivial and unassuming show cause such pandemonium? You are surprised when the first act closes without any rising action or revelation. The lights rise for the intermission, and you consider leaving early, stifling a yawn. Before you are able to decide, however, you find yourself drifting… drifting… to sleep.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to <b>Scenario I: The Tatterdemalion</b>.</p>"},oe={alienAid:{readyAndMoveMiGoScientist:"Ready Mi-Go Scientist and move it to any location"},arrivalOfTheKing:{memoriesToCrossOut:"Cross out any amount of tally marks next to your “Memories”"},biologyLab:{healDamage:"Heal 1 damage from each investigator at your location",healHorror:"Heal 1 horror from each investigator at your location"},contamination:{discardAlly:"Discard the attached Ally",placeDoom:"Place 1 doom on the attached Ally"},delights:{doNotRemoveAToken:"Do not remove a token",removeSkull:"Remove a Skull token from the chaos bag",removeCultist:"Remove a Cultist token from the chaos bag",removeTablet:"Remove a Tablet token from the chaos bag",removeElderThing:"Remove an Elder Thing token from the chaos bag",removeElderSign:"Remove an Elder Sign token from the chaos bag"},desync:{traumaAndExile:"Suffer 1 mental trauma and add 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”, then exile this card",returnToDeck:"If your deck has 5 or more cards in it, shuffle this card back into your deck. Otherwise, discard it"},evaSuit:{doNotPutIntoPlay:"Do not put EVA Suit into play"},fromTheDark:{takeDamage:"Take {count} damage",drawAMimic:"Search the encounter deck and discard pile for a Mimic enemy and draw it"},innocentMishap:{damageNearestBrain:"Deal 1 damage to the nearest Brain story asset",damageMiGoScientist:"Deal 2 damage to Mi-Go Scientist",take2DirectDamage:"Take 2 direct damage"},jv7Hyades:{trefoil:"Scan for the clover icon",t:"Scan for the T icon"},medicalFoam:{doNotPutIntoPlay:"Do not put Medical Foam into play"},micrometeoroid:{discardEachEvent:"Discard each event in your hand"},mindMachineInterface:{doNotPutIntoPlay:"Do not put Mind-Machine Interface into play"},paleBlueDot:{takeHorror:"Take 1 horror",placeDoom:"Add 1 doom to the current agenda and discard this card"},paradoxicalThreat:{placeFacedown:"Place the top 3 cards of the encounter deck into your threat area, face-down",doomAndDraw:"Add 1 doom to the current agenda and draw 3 face-down cards from your threat area"},radiationTablets:{doNotPutIntoPlay:"Do not put Radiation Tablets into play"},sceneShifting:{placeDoom:"Place 1 doom on the current agenda",moveEnemies:"Move each enemy 1 location toward you. Each enemy at your location immediately attacks you"},solarEclipse:{take1Horror:"Take 1 horror",locationGets2Shroud:"Your location gets +2 shroud for this investigation"},surprise:{moveBoogeyman:"Move The Boogeyman to your current location",boogeymanAttacks:"The Boogeyman immediately attacks you"},virtualAccessKey:{addToDeck:"Add Virtual Access Key to your deck",doNotAddToDeck:"Do not add it to your deck"},whatTypeOfShipIsThis:{placeDoom:"Place 1 doom on the current agenda and add this to the victory display",removeFromGame:"Remove this card from the game"},withoutATrace:{assumeCommandOfTheShip:"Assume command of the ship",scavengeTheShipForParts:"Scavenge the ship for parts"}},ae={youWereTransportedToTheVirtualDreamlandsByMaja:"You were transported to the Virtual Dreamlands by Maja.",youEnteredTheVirtualDreamlandsByYourOwnMeans:"You entered the Virtual Dreamlands by your own means.",hasBeenInfectedByTheCybervirus:"Has been infected by the cybervirus.",youAreTrappedInAVirtualNightmare:"You are trapped in a virtual nightmare.",youPartiallyRestoredTheSanityOfK2PS187:"You partially restored the sanity of K2-PS187.",youFullyRestoredTheSanityOfK2PS187:"You fully restored the sanity of K2-PS187.",youHaveWatchedThePerformanceOfHeirToCarcosa:"You have watched the performance of Heir to Carcosa.",theElbrusStationHasBeenLostInTheQuantumRealm:"The Elbrus Station has been lost in the quantum realm.",theElbrusStationHasBeenFullyStabilized:"The Elbrus Station has been fully stabilized.",youHaveWitnessedThePrimordialChaos:"You have witnessed the primordial chaos.",youHaveRescuedTheRemainingCrewOfTheNostalgiaII:"You have rescued the remaining crew of the Nostalgia II.",theNostalgiaIIHasBeenSaved:"The Nostalgia II has been saved.",youCouldntSaveTheCrewOfTheNostalgiaII:"You couldn’t save the crew of the Nostalgia II.",allInvestigatorsHaveBeenCorruptedByTheEarth:"All investigators have been corrupted by the Earth.",youAreNotInGoodStandingWithTheMiGo:"You are not in good standing with the Mi-Go.",youAreAlliedWithTheMiGo:"You are allied with the Mi-Go.",youHaveUncoveredTheCultistsInhumanMethods:"You have uncovered the cultist’s inhuman methods.",youHaveWitnessedTheUnconsciousPandemonium:"You have witnessed the unconscious pandemonium.",youHaveWitnessedTheManifestedMadness:"You have witnessed the manifested madness.",theInvestigatorsAreTrappedWithinCarcosa:"The investigators are trapped within Carcosa.",theInvestigatorsKnowOfTheAbjurationOfTheThrone:"The investigators know of the Abjuration of the Throne.",theSunWentSupernovaAndWipedOutMostOfTheSolarSystem:"The sun went supernova and wiped out most of the solar system.",miGoSafelyReturnedToTheirHomeWorld:"Mi-Go safely returned to their home world.",hopeWasShieldedFromTheBlast:"Hope was shielded from the blast.",theUCCEscapedToAnotherGalaxy:"The UCC escaped to another galaxy.",livedTheRemainderOfTheirDaysWithHope:"Lived the remainder of their days, with Hope.",livedTheRemainderOfTheirDaysOnParadise:"Lived the remainder of their days, on Paradise.",youHaveReturnedToThePalacesOfDimCarcosa:"You have returned to the palaces of Dim Carcosa.",wasCaughtInTheSupernovasBlast:"Was caught in the supernova’s blast.",theInvestigatorsEscapedHastursGrasp:"The investigators have finally escaped Hastur’s grasp and prevented him from escaping his prison.",theRealmOfCarcosaOvertookOurUniverse:"The realm of Carcosa overtook our universe, and Tassilda rules over the black stars.",hasturAndTassildaAreImprisonedInCarcosaOnceMore:"Hastur and Tassilda are imprisoned in Carcosa once more, and the universe vanquished the inevitable… For now.",impendingDoom:"Impending Doom",memories:"Memories"},ie={label:{noInvestigatorAddsK2:"No investigator adds it to their deck"}},ot={name:U,xp:Q,intro:J,specialRules:Z,additionalRulesAndClarifications:ee,prologue:te,label:oe,key:ae,electricNightmare:ie},at=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,additionalRulesAndClarifications:ee,default:ot,electricNightmare:ie,intro:J,key:ae,label:oe,name:U,prologue:te,specialRules:Z,xp:Q},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),ne=JSON.parse(`{"setup":{"gatherSets":"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Electric Nightmare</i>, <i>Endtimes</i>, and <i>Dark Past</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/electric-nightmare.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/endtimes.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/dark-past.png' /></section>","setAsideBoogeyman":"Set aside the <i>The Boogeyman</i> encounter set, out of play. This set is indicated by the following icon:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/the-boogeyman.png' /></section>","randomizeAct":"Randomly select one version of act 1 (Public School 187) to put into play. Remove the other two versions from the game.","setAsideLocations":"Set each copy of Undefined Room locations aside, out of play, as well as the Entrance Hall (A Shimmer in the Wall).","placeSchoolGrounds":"Put the School Grounds location into play.","startAt":"Each investigator begins play at the School Grounds.","attachMaja":"Attach the Maja story asset to School Grounds.","setAsideStoryAssets":"Set the following story assets aside, out of play: Alma, David, Tilde, William, and each copy of K2-PS187.","checkCampaignLog":"Check your Campaign Log. If an investigator *has been infected by the cybervirus*, that investigator must search the collection for Cybervirus and begin the scenario with it in their hand."},"specialRules":[{"title":"Locations in the Virtual Dreamlands","body":"<p class='basic'>During this scenario, locations will be arranged in schematics, depicted by their icons. Locations are adjacent orthogonally (left, right, above, and below), and are not adjacent diagonally.</p>"},{"title":"Switching Locations","body":"<p class='basic'>Throughout this scenario, you may be instructed to switch two locations with each other. When a location is switched with another location, they take each other’s place in the arrangement. All tokens, attachments, investigators, enemies, and other cards at each location remain on the same location (they have “moved” with the location — only the arrangement and connections have changed).</p><p class='basic'><i>For example, if Wendy Adams is currently in the School Grounds and is instructed to switch her location with the Entrance Hall, which is directly above the School Grounds, the positions of the two locations will be switched. After switching these two locations with each other, Wendy Adams remains in the School Grounds, now above the Entrance Hall.</i></p>"},{"title":"Swarming","body":"<p class='basic'>An enemy with swarm cards underneath is actually a pack of enemies operating in unison. The enemy that the swarm cards are underneath is called the “host enemy”. In this scenario, encounter cards can become swarm cards. When those swarm cards are defeated, they are discarded into the encounter discard pile.</p><ul><li>Each swarm card underneath the host enemy acts as a separate instance of that enemy for most purposes. Each swarm card has the same values and text as its host card.</li><li>Each swarm card attacks separately when enemies attack during the enemy phase. Once the host enemy and all of its swarm cards have attacked during this step, exhaust all of them.</li><li>Each swarm card can be attacked or dealt damage separately, but the host enemy cannot be defeated while it still has swarm cards underneath it. When a swarm card is defeated, any excess damage may be dealt to another swarm card underneath the same host enemy or to the host enemy itself.</li><li>The host enemy and all of its swarm cards move, engage, and exhaust as a single entity. <i>(For example, if a host enemy or any of its swarm cards are evaded, all of them exhaust and become disengaged.)</i></li></ul>"}],"intro":{"title":"Scenario II: Electric Nightmare","body":"<p>You struggle to follow the pace of the little girl as she skips and hops towards the small town. “My name is Maja. My directive is to store and manage the information archives on the ship.” She hastily explains that a few of her classmates and her were kidnapped from their school by the “bad people” on January 16th, 2045. Their brains were surgically removed and preserved in a special experimental machine that eventually became the powerful supercomputer operating the Tatterdemalion, K2-PS187.</p><p>As you walk through the town, it becomes clear that something horrible has happened here. Everything appears to be in disarray, as if a riot has recently passed through. Freshly-painted yellow graffiti depicting strange symbols and hieroglyphs can be seen. Everywhere are splatters of blood, spent shell casings, and pale face masks. There are no bodies, but you can hear the sound of distant screams, gunshots, and sirens coming from beyond the streets. Nearby is an overturned police car and a black box truck lying on its side. Huge claw marks have torn into the metal of the truck and its rear doors hang open. As you walk past, a radio from within crackles and sputters, then blares, “Hello, Unit 12? Unit 12, is that you? Please respond.” Maja clarifies that this virtual environment that represents K2-PS187’s dreams takes the form of the day they got captured, the day the entire world ended. What could possibly have happened on Earth in the distant future? Or rather, the distant past?</p><p>You finally arrive outside of a large brick building. Maja halts and gestures towards it. “This is where my friends are hiding. The bad people made us translate a scary story and make a movie for them. We didn’t want to read it, but they made us. A few days later, Annie, the universal translator, she – she –” Maja struggles to utter the words. There is a desperate fear in her eyes. “You won’t believe me, but I swear, it was the Boogeyman! I saw the Boogeyman eat her! I ran away and searched the archives to see if anything, anyone could help. After a long time, I finally found someone and called out to them. That’s when you woke up! Now that you’re inside our system, you can save us!”</p><p>Before you is a path leading to a pair of double doors, above which are the words “Public School 187.” Underneath, someone has written “HASTUR RISES!” in yellow spray paint. An inhuman howl echoes through the halls inside the school, followed by children screaming in terror.</p><p class='basic'>Check the Campaign Log. Each investigator with 3 or fewer “Memories” must read <b>Desynchronization</b>.</p>"},"tooltips":{"cafeteria":{"investigate":"_{'{'}action{'}'} Investigate_. This test gets +2 difficulty. If you succeed, discover an additional clue from an adjacent location."}},"resolutions":{"noResolution":{"title":"No Resolution Was Reached","body":"If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated):","proceedToResolution1":"If there are no Reintegrated story cards in the victory display: Proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.","proceedToResolution2":"If there is at least 1 Reintegrated story card when the scenario ended: Proceed to <b>Resolution 2</b>."},"resolution1":{"title":"Resolution 1","body":"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> A roar of applause startles you awake. The crowd of the theatre rises to their feet, cheering endlessly. Several patrons in the front row are throwing roses to the actors on stage, who are bowing with wide smiles across their faces. A searing headache crawls through your temples. How did you get back here? Were you in the theatre all along? What about the spaceship? The virtual reality? Was it all just a terrible dream? Before you can get up and exit the auditorium, the lights flicker off. A spotlight shines onto the stage, illuminating a single actor, dressed up as a clown. Something must have gone wrong inside the simulation. You are no longer inside of K2-PS187’s nightmare, but your own. Without outside interference, your body will likely be drifting in endless space forever, as your mind slowly decays in this rotten reproduction of reality. The stranger begins laughing. A horrible, ear-piercing laugh.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you are trapped in a virtual nightmare</i>.</li><li>Each investigator is driven <b>insane</b>.</li><li>The investigators lose the campaign.</li></ul>"},"resolution2":{"title":"Resolution 2","body":"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> You wake up inside of a virtual classroom, surrounded by the children you rescued. The children themselves, who at first appeared dirty and disheveled, now appear clean and neat in school uniforms. They contained the insanity of the remaining children by creating a new pocket reality, disconnected from the system mainframe. The survivors mourn the loss of their friends, but are glad that there is no more Boogeyman to scare them and that there are no more bad people to tell them what to do. The virtual dreamscape is no longer a nightmarish hell it used to be.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you partially restored the sanity of K2-PS187</i>.</li><li>Check the number of Reintegrated story cards in the victory display. If there is exactly 1, an investigator may add the K2-PS187 (25% Functionality) permanent story asset to their deck; if there are exactly 2, the K2-PS187 (50% Functionality) story asset; if there are exactly 3, the K2-PS187 (75% Functionality) story asset.</li><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Interlude I: Mission Briefing</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution3":{"title":"Resolution 3","body":"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> Outside, the sun comes out and it appears to be a beautiful spring day. Inside, the halls are clean and orderly, with brightly painted pictures on the walls. The children themselves, who at first appeared dirty and disheveled, now appear clean and neat in school uniforms. They are overjoyed that the Boogeyman and all the bad people are finally gone. They understand that they can never return home and that their families are long dead. But that does not diminish their happiness that there is no more Boogeyman to scare them and that they have a real teacher to take care of them again. The virtual dreamscape is now filled with happy, loving children.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you fully restored the sanity of K2-PS187</i>.</li><li>An investigator may choose to add the K2-PS187 (100% Functionality) permanent story asset to their deck.</li><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Interlude I: Mission Briefing</b>.</li></ul>"}},"desynchronization":{"title":"Desynchronization","body":"<p>An overturned schoolbus gathers dust on the school grounds. As you examine the vandalized windows, you notice a glimpse of your own reflection. However, you no longer recognize the person looking back at you. The frame, the distinct facial features, they all seem so familiar to you, yet you know this is not your body. You stare into the glass in disbelief. The face of your reflection morphs into a blank, pale mask with no mouth, nose or eyes. The virtual reality no longer recognizes your residual self image anymore – the mental projection of your digital self has decayed into nothingness.</p><ul><li>You must add the Desync weakness to your deck. This card does not count towards your deck limit.</li></ul>"}}`),it={electricNightmare:ne},nt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:it,electricNightmare:ne},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),se={intro:{title:"Scenario V: Fragment of Carcosa",body:"<p>There is no time to waste. As if it were muscle-memory, you adorn the makeshift shrine by installing one of the quantum shards in the center. Several of the golden discs obtained from the Mi-Go must be placed in front — aligned to form a syzygy. With the components in order, you pronounce the unspeakable message from Earth:</p><p class='center'>“Let the red dawn surmise<br>What we shall do,<br>When this blue starlight dies<br>And all is through.”</p><p>The golden discs begin trembling, building momentum until they all turn upright and begin to roll around the shrine in one direction. The quantum artifact’s hue shifts into a yellow glare before glowing an intense and dense red. The discs spin around and around the surface at different, but consistent speeds, until they finally slow down to a crawl and fall over simultaneously. Then, as suddenly as it began, the red shard erupts in a fog of nebulous gas, blinding you in its flurry.</p><p>When your eyesight returns, all that remains are the golden discs resting at various locations across the floor. You instinctively recognize this as a schematic of the solar system. Upon closer examination, a single remnant of the purple shard remains between what you believe is Jupiter and Saturn’s orbits. K2-PS187 confirms that the depiction is accurate to the current star-time — and begins plotting a course towards the asteroid.</p><p>On the way there, you think of the different worlds you have visited and many adventures you have experienced, both in this world and in your own. Throughout every interaction, every quest, is the underlying sense of hope and optimism for the future. This future does not deserve to become another pawn to the mad king, and you intend to stop that from happening.</p><p>When you arrive, the asteroid does not resemble what you had expected. The egg-shaped asteroid is about 4 km at its widest, and looks awfully… normal. The yellow color is closer to a murky brown than gold. It is littered with craters and cavities, battered by the harshness of space. Without delay, you suit on and descend onto the surface of Fragment, ready to face the Royal Princess of Carcosa…</p>"},setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Fragment of Carcosa</i> and <i>Inhabitants of Carcosa</i> <i>(from The Path to Carcosa)</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/fragment-of-carcosa.png' /><img src='{setImgPath}/inhabitants-of-carcosa.png' /></section>",placeLocations:"Put the Surface of Fragment and Abandoned Lander locations into play.",startAt:"Each investigator begins play at Surface of Fragment.",setAsideLocations:"Set aside the 6 double-sided locations, out of play.",setAsideStoryCards:"Set aside the 4 one-sided story cards (Delights, Arrival of the King, For You Alone and Lost Expedition), out of play.",setAsideCards:"Set aside the Bottle of Whispers story asset, the Cave Dweller enemy, the Beast of Aldebaran enemy, and each copy of Spawn of Hali aside, out of play."},tokens:{easyStandard:{skull:"-2. If you fail while you are at a *Cave* location, take 1 damage.",cultist:"-2. If you fail while you are at a *Carcosa* location, take 1 horror.",tablet:"-1. You must either (choose one): Reveal another token, or cross out 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”.",elderThing:"-2. If you are at a *Carcosa* location: Add 1 doom to the current agenda, or automatically fail this skill test."},hardExpert:{skull:"-3. If you are at a *Cave* location, take 1 damage.",cultist:"-3. If you are at a *Carcosa* location, take 1 horror.",tablet:"-2. You must either (choose one): Reveal another token, or cross out 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”.",elderThing:"-3. If you are at a *Carcosa* location: Add 1 doom to the current agenda, or automatically fail this skill test."}},specialRules:[{title:"Flipping Locations in Fragment",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, you may be instructed to flip a location to its other side. When this occurs, simply flip the location, keeping all tokens, attachments, investigators, enemies, and other cards on that same location (which will have a different name). Then, add clues on that location up to its clue value.</p><p class='basic'>Locations with “Cannot be flipped.” will simply ignore the instructions to flip it, and will not prevent abilities from triggering.</p>"}],label:{tablet:{revealAnotherToken:"Reveal another token",crossOffMemory:"Cross out 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”"}},resolutions:{noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"If each investigator was defeated:",proceedToResolution1:"If it is act 1 or act 2, proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.",proceedToResolution2:"If it is act 3, proceed to <b>Resolution 2</b>."},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> When you finally awaken, in the distance, the alien spires of a warped city rise into the clouds. Behind you, the dark surface of a lake reflects the glare of two suns. You call out to K2-PS187 for help, but there is no response this time. This isn’t another simulation; you are imprisoned in the realm of Carcosa, with no way out to save the solar system.</p><ul><li>Record in your Campaign Log that <i>the investigators are trapped within Carcosa</i>.</li><li>Each investigator is driven <b>insane</b>.</li><li>The investigators lose the campaign.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> You wake up in a cold sweat back in the cryo-chamber. While you are confused and disoriented, K2-PS187 explains that you have been in a coma for over 2 months after you decided to enter your own mind. Your experience on that asteroid, the true nature of Hastur—it was too real to be imagined; it must have been forged from fragments of the cultist’s memories. Regardless of the circumstances, you now know of the impending doom of the solar system, and understand what you must do: save as many as you can before the inevitable.</p><ul><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 2 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario VI: Starfall</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"Resolution 3",body:"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> When you finally regroup back on the Tatterdemalion, all you can think of is all the time you could have saved if only you remembered the real threat you face. The sun only has a few years left to shine, and most of humanity is oblivious to its imminent demise. In the face of this impending doom, you know what you must do: save as many as you can before the inevitable.</p><ul><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario VI: Starfall</b>.</li></ul>"}}},st={fragmentOfCarcosa:se},rt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:st,fragmentOfCarcosa:se},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),re={intro:{title:"Scenario IIIb: In the Shadow of Earth",body:"<p>“In the middle of the 21st century, Earth was in complete chaos. Rioting, crime, madness and worse had become the order of the day for the entire world. [...] In a last ditch of effort, two of the Arks were completed and the third vessel was stripped for parts. The two completed vessels set out for Mars, each carrying 3000 humans in suspended animation. One vessel, the Liberty, suffered a massive power plant failure and the crew and passengers were killed. The other ship, Hope, eventually reached Mars...”</p><p class='basic right'>— Maja, Information Archives</p><p>The planet Earth — what used to be humanity’s sanctuary, is now abandoned to the madness of the Ancient Ones. There is very little information of what remains on the Earth, but if anyone would attempt to send out a transmission, survey vessels stationed around the planet such as the Nostalgia II would hear those calls.</p><p>The trip itself was uneventful, and you spend your days watching the blue dot of Earth grow and grow in size. Around the time you can finally recognize a few of the continents, the Tatterdemalion picks up a lonely and distant beat — the echo of the Nostalgia II’s distress beacon. You try to hail the crew with your radios, but there is no response. The Tatterdemalion begins its deceleration, and with no time to waste, you prepare to board the godforsaken ship.</p>"},setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>In the Shadow of Earth</i> and <i>Deep Space</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/in-the-shadow-of-earth.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/deep-space.png' /></section>",setAsideEnemies:"Set aside the The Entity and The Feaster from Afar enemies.",createScanningDeck:"Create the scanning deck. This is done by taking all the other encounter cards with icons at the bottom of their back side and shuffling them together.",createEvidenceDeck:"Create the facedown “Evidence” deck. This is done by taking all the one sided story cards and shuffling them together.",placeLocations:"Put all remaining locations into play. Each investigator begins play at the Airlocks.",setAsideEvidence:"Without looking at it, put the top card of the “Evidence” deck facedown under the scenario reference card. Repeat this process once for every 3 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log. <i>(Example: If you had 5 Impending Doom, you would put a total of 2 cards under the scenario reference card.)</i>"},tokens:{easyStandard:{skull:"-X. X is half the amount of damage on you and assets you control (rounded down).",cultist:"-2. If you fail, deal 1 damage or 1 horror to an *Ally* asset you control.",tablet:"Reveal another token. If you fail, take 1 damage and 1 horror.",elderThing:"0. You must either (choose one): Take 2 damage, or this test automatically fails."},hardExpert:{skull:"-X. X is half the amount of damage on you and assets you control (rounded up).",cultist:"-3. If you fail, deal 1 damage or 1 horror to an *Ally* asset you control.",tablet:"-1. Reveal another token. If you fail, take 1 damage and 1 horror.",elderThing:"0. You must either (choose one): Take 3 damage, or this test automatically fails."}},specialRules:[{title:"Cards Removed from the Game",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, you must keep track of cards that are removed from the game. Put any cards removed from the game in an area out of play that is still accessible.</p>"},{title:"Motion Scanning",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, the <b>Scan</b> action designator functions slightly differently. <b>You may only scan when you are at a location with an icon matching the top card of the scanning deck.</b> When you scan, instead of searching for the topmost card of the scanning deck matching the icon you are scanning for, simply draw the top card of the scanning deck. As such, you will have to move around the ship and follow the icons depicted on the top card of the scanning deck.</p>"}],resolutions:{noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"<p><b>If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated):</b></p><ul><li>If the current act is Act 3, proceed to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li><li>Otherwise, proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> You barely made it out of the madhouse alive. The horrors you’ve seen of what remains of the crew is almost too much for you to handle.</p><ul><li>If there are no <b>Crew</b> story assets in the victory display: Proceed directly to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li><li>If there are <b>Crew</b> story assets in the victory display: Look at the story cards that are under the scenario reference card but do not read them. For each of the story cards, reveal 1 random chaos token from the chaos bag. If it is <i>not</i> a {'{'}elderSign{'}'}, {'{'}bless{'}'}, ‘+1’, or ‘0’ token, the <b>Crew</b> story asset corresponding to that story card is an imitation of the Entity!<ul><li>If any of the <b>Crew</b> story assets that are imitations are in the victory display: Proceed to <b>Resolution 2</b>.</li><li>If none of the <b>Crew</b> story assets that are imitations are in the victory display: Proceed to <b>Resolution 3</b>.</li></ul></li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> A horrible scream echoes through the halls of the Tatterdemalion. One of the crew members you’ve brought aboard was an imitation! They revealed themselves and consumed all the crew members you could have saved. You were eventually able to fight it off and eject it through an airlock. However, the damage is considerable and has set back your mission by many months.</p><ul><li>Proceed to <b>Resolution 5</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"Resolution 3",body:"<p><b>Resolution 3:</b> You managed to save some of the crew, and they mourn the lost for several days. Thankfully, none of the crew members you have brought aboard was an imitation. Over time, they describe how the madness only began a few days after they decoded a transmission from Earth — a cryptic poem.</p><blockquote><i>“Let the red dawn surmise<br/>What we shall do,<br/>When this blue starlight dies<br/>And all is through.”</i></blockquote><p>You believe this poem must be what the cultists were after — but it is meaningless to you and doesn’t help you uncover the coordinates of Fragment.</p><p>You finally deliver the remaining crew to a service station in the Martian orbit, and the survivors thank you once more for saving them and bids farewell. Despite all, you must leave this behind you and look forwards towards another lead.</p><ul><li>Record in your Campaign Log that <i>you have rescued the remaining crew of the Nostalgia II</i>.</li><li>Add 1 tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log. Then, add 1 additional tally mark for every 2 <b>Crew</b> story asset removed from the game, attached to the Entity, or in the scanning deck.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><b>Experience</b>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Return to <b>The Search for Fragment</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution4:{title:"Resolution 4",body:"<p><b>Resolution 4:</b> The remaining crew of the Nostalgia II thank you for your help in defeating the abomination. They describe how the madness only began a few days after they decoded a transmission from Earth — a cryptic poem.</p><blockquote><i>“Let the red dawn surmise<br/>What we shall do,<br/>When this blue starlight dies<br/>And all is through.”</i></blockquote><p>You believe this poem must be what the cultists were after — but it is meaningless to you and doesn’t help you uncover the coordinates of Fragment.</p><p>Despite all, you must leave this behind you and look forwards towards another lead.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>The Nostalgia II has been saved</i>.</li><li>An investigator may add the Space Artillery story asset to their deck. This card does not count towards that investigator’s deck limit.</li><li>Add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign for catching the eye of the King in Yellow.</li><li>Add 1 tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log. Then, add 1 additional tally mark for every 2 <b>Crew</b> story asset attached to the Entity.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display and of each <b>Crew</b> story asset that the investigators control.<ul><li><b>Experience</b>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Return to <b>The Search for Fragment</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution5:{title:"Resolution 5",body:"<p><b>Resolution 5:</b> You couldn’t save anyone. The one silver lining — during the ordeal, K2-PS187 was able to hack into the mainframe and uncover what the cultists retrieved, a cryptic message received from Earth. You spend some time attempting to decode the message — but to no avail. You must leave this decryption, and the traumatic experiences associated with it, behind for now and look forwards toward another lead.</p><ul><li>Record in your Campaign Log that <i>you couldn’t save the crew of the Nostalgia II</i>.</li><li>Record in your Campaign Log that <i>all investigators have been corrupted by the Earth</i>.</li><li>Add 4 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display. Each investigator earns 2 additional experience as they have seen the unthinkable.<ul><li><b>Experience</b>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Return to <b>The Search for Fragment</b>.</li></ul>"}}},ht={inTheShadowOfEarth:re},lt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:ht,inTheShadowOfEarth:re},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),he={1:"Mission Briefing",2:"The Search for Fragment",3:"Introspection"},le={interludes:{2:"Interlude",3:"Interlude II"}},de={title:"Interlude I: Mission Briefing",missionBriefing1:"<p>_Mission Briefing 1:_ The virtual dreamscape around you swirls into a flurry of ephemeral blue code and dissipates into complete darkness. You find yourself back inside the Tatterdemalion. A sharp sting hurts you as a mechanical arm unplugs the cyber-cable out of the back of your head. K2-PS187 apologizes for the intrusive method it used to bring you into the virtual dreamlands and is now fully cooperative. The cybernetic supercomputer will help you in any way it can, starting with a summary of the recent events that have unfolded on the Tatterdemalion.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _Mission Briefing 3_.</p>",missionBriefing2:"<p>_Mission Briefing 2:_ The virtual dreamscape around you swirls into a flurry of ephemeral blue and dissipates away as you disconnect from the virtual dreamscape and stumble out of the all too familiar cryosleep chamber. K2-PS187 is now fully cooperative and will help you in any way it can. The supercomputer starts by briefing you on the recent events that have unfolded on the Tatterdemalion.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _Mission Briefing 3_.</p>",missionBriefing3:"<p>_Mission Briefing 3:_ The crew of Tatterdemalion was composed of worshippers of Hastur, one of the Ancient Ones that has descended upon Earth. The cultists recently undertook a mission to free Tassilda, daughter of Hastur, rumored to be imprisoned on an asteroid codenamed Fragment. The ship managed to rendezvous with Fragment and deployed several survey teams to search the caverns upon it. Before your current mind was implanted, you were one of these cultist explorers, destined to awaken Tassilda.</p><p>After a few weeks of survey, one of the teams retrieved a slab of alien hieroglyphs, and ordered K2-PS187 to begin a translation. Another team reported to have found the inner chambers where Tassilda resided and destroyed the imprisoning sigils. They were never heard from again.</p><p>You and your fellow cultists swiftly withdrew from the asteroid before the princess of Carcosa could awaken and attack the Tatterdemalion. Content that such were the risks one took worshipping gods of pure chaos, you did not mourn your lost companions. The ship was set to return to the inner solar system. Your mission has been a success. You had finally freed Tassilda, the daughter of Hastur, who might soon be elevated by her father to become a new Ancient One.</p><p>While most of the cultists entered cryosleep for the journey home, K2-PS187 was busy analysing the alien runes. When the translation was complete, the computer learned of a story titled “Heir to Carcosa.” The knowledge caused it to go insane and slaughter all of the waking crew out of terror. The ship was left in turmoil, drifting without sense through space — until K2-PS187 brought you back into this world from the archives in a final cry for help.</p><p>You now understand what you must do. Although Earth is no longer the home it used to be, humanity still exists, spread out throughout colonies in the solar system, living in fear and in isolation. If the being named Tassilda, Heir to Carcosa, would be exalted by her father, there is no doubt that she will decide to reign over humanity’s colonies with the madness of Carcosa. You must atone for your past sins and eliminate the entity before she can be elevated to godhood. Unfortunately, the last recorded positions of Fragment were among the data lost during the initial corruption. However, K2-PS187 was able to retrieve a few leads from the ship’s itinerary. You will need to traverse the solar system to locate the coordinates of the asteroid and prevent Tassilda’s ascension.</p>",simulatedPerformance:"<p class='basic'>The investigators may choose to watch a simulated performance of the translated play. If you do so, read _Heir to Carcosa_.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _The Search for Fragment_.</p>",label:{watchThePerformance:"Watch a simulated performance of Heir to Carcosa. READ AT YOUR OWN RISK.",declineToWatch:"Do not watch the performance."},checkCampaignLog:"<p class='basic'>Check the Campaign Log. *If you were transported to the Virtual Dreamlands by Maja*, read _Mission Briefing 1_. Otherwise, skip to _Mission Briefing 2_.</p>"},ce={title:"Interlude I: Mission Briefing",body:"<section class='note-green'><h1>Heir to Carcosa</h1><h3 class='term' style='text-align:center;width:100%;'>READ AT YOUR OWN RISK.</h3><p>The program begins with the royal family of Yhtill cowering before the King in Yellow, Avatar of Hastur. For the next three hours, you witness a horrifying creative work, full of betrayal, intrigue, and horror. The story unfolds thus:</p><p>After claiming Yhtill and absorbing it into Carcosa, the King in Yellow took the insane princess Camilla as a consort. Before her death, the princess bore the Ancient One three children, who became fosterlings of Hastur. They were two boys, named Thothut and Tasylock, and a girl named Tassilda. While normal-seeming at first, the children developed many of the physical characteristics and powers of their father. This transformation was viewed by their mother as yet another of Carcosa’s many corruptions. It was the final blow to Camilla’s mind, causing her heart to stop from despair and grief.</p><p>For some time the royal trio lived with their sire in Carcosa, evil beings serving loyally at the foot of their father. But soon, like their mother, uncle, and grandmother before them, the princes and princess of Carcosa began to whisper, squabble, and plot. They had dreams of power and succession. Eventually Thothut and Tasylock unwisely moved against their father. Hastur was aware of the plot all along, and easily avoided their traps. In a way too horrible to describe, he destroyed both of his sons.</p><p>His daughter Tassilda, who knew of her siblings’ plot but refused to take part in it, was spared. But she had done nothing to warn her father, choosing to wait and see if their plot was successful before committing to a course of action. For her silent betrayal, Tassilda was punished. Her father, He Who Should Not Be Named, sealed her into her home, which the Ancient One tore free of Carcosa and hurled out into space. Her father claimed that in an inevitable time, she will be released, and granted all that she desires.</p><ul><li>Record in your Campaign Log that *you have watched the performance of Heir to Carcosa*.</li><li>Each investigator suffers 1 mental trauma.</li></ul></section><section class='note-green'><ul><li>If an investigator controls the Heir to Carcosa weakness, they may add 2 tally marks next to their “Memories”.</li></ul></section>",label:{addTwoMemories:"Add 2 tally marks next to your “Memories”.",doNotAddMemories:"Do not add tally marks."}},ue={title:"The Search for Fragment",body:"<p>Aboard the Tatterdemalion, you and your companions seek the coordinates of the asteroid “Fragment” to prevent the ascension of Tassilda, daughter of Hastur. Upon analysing the remaining data aboard the ship, K2-PS187 and you have decided on 3 traces that are worth investigating. However, time is of the essence — you may want to visit the destination you think will be the most valuable first.</p><p class='basic'>The investigators must choose to follow one of the following traces that have not already been chosen. If you cannot (you have already completed each Scenario III), skip to _Interlude II: Introspection_.</p>",trace1:"<div class='green trace'><p>_Trace 1:_ The last destination of the Tatterdemalion before travelling to Fragment was a research laboratory on a stray asteroid named Elbrus. This specific facility was built to study and experiment with the materials that exhibit quantum-like behaviour. You aren't sure what the cultists were hoping to achieve there, but perhaps these scientists can steer you in the right direction.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _Scenario IIIa: Lost Quantum_.</p></div>",trace2:"<div class='green trace'><p>_Trace 2:_ Thorough analysis of the archives has revealed evidence of hacking into the mainframe of an Earth survey vessel named the Nostalgia II, and several references to a “quarantine” and to “trust no one”. If you can establish contact with the crew, maybe you can figure out what the cultists were looking for.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _Scenario IIIb: In the Shadow of Earth_.</p></div>",trace3:"<div class='green trace'><p>_Trace 3:_ The Tatterdemalion appears to have landed on one of Saturn’s moons several times in the past few years. The ship’s log record these operations as “negotiations.” K2-PS187 notes that this is particularly strange, as there are no known human outposts this far out in the solar system. You could pay a visit to these coordinates to figure out what these “negotiations” consist of.</p><p class='basic right'>Proceed to _Scenario IIIc: Strange Moons_.</p></div>",label:{lostQuantum:"Follow Trace 1. Proceed to Scenario IIIa: Lost Quantum.",inTheShadowOfEarth:"Follow Trace 2. Proceed to Scenario IIIb: In the Shadow of Earth.",strangeMoons:"Follow Trace 3. Proceed to Scenario IIIc: Strange Moons."}},pe={title:"Interlude II: Introspection",body:"<p>The strange quantum shards, the golden disks obtained from the Mi-Go, the cryptic message from Earth… Despite travelling throughout the solar system to uncover these individual pieces of the puzzle, you still can’t seem to fit them together into one big picture. There is a key element missing – a connective tissue that will make sense of it all. Of course, there is also still one place you know for certain contains all of your answers, but you fear what you may find there. And that place is your own mind. Deep within your own subconscious, you can feel a shimmer of the cultist you embody – imprisoned in the edges between your thoughts. You know for certain that the other version of you remembers how to find Fragment. Entering one’s own virtual mind is particularly dangerous as any small mistake could send you spiraling into insanity. But you are ready to confront your past once and for all. With the help of K2-PS187, the cryo-chamber’s dream protocols are once again tinkered with to access your own personal memories this time. You lie back down in the cryo-chamber once more. With a flick of a switch, you begin to fall back into unconsciousness…</p>",searchTheTatterdemalion:"<p class='basic'>The investigators may choose to take their time to search the Tatterdemalion for any more important details they may have missed. If you do so, add 1 tally mark to “Impending Doom” and to each investigator’s “Memories.”</p>",sideStory:"<p class='basic'>The investigators may choose to enter a simulation of the Earth’s histories to learn more about this future by playing a side-story, crossing out “Memories” instead of paying its experience cost. Experience earned by playing the side-story become “Memories” for investigators instead. (Return to this section of the campaign guide after finishing the side-story.) <i>Resolve this manually if desired, adjusting “Memories” in the campaign log accordingly.</i></p>",chaosTokens:"<p class='basic'>Based on your difficulty level, add the following chaos token(s) to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign:</p><ul class='basic'><li>Easy: –3.</li><li>Standard: –5.</li><li>Hard: –6 and {'{'}elderThing{'}'}.</li><li>Expert: –7 and {'{'}elderThing{'}'}.</li></ul>",checkCampaignLog:"<p class='basic'>Check the Campaign Log. *If the investigators have uncovered the cultist’s inhuman methods:* Proceed to _Introspection 1_.</p><p class='basic'>Otherwise, skip to _Scenario IV: The Machine in Yellow_.</p>",introspection1:"<p>Memories of your past life come flooding back to you – horrible visions of launching missiles onto mining outposts, spreading memetic biological viruses, and other unspeakable evils upon humanity. The cultist that you used to be must answer for their atrocities – and you are more than ready to finally extinguish their presence within you.</p><p class='basic'>Each investigator begins the following scenario with 1 additional resource and 1 additional card in their starting hand.</p>",label:{searchTheShip:"Search the Tatterdemalion. Add 1 tally mark to “Impending Doom” and to each investigator’s “Memories.”",doNotSearchTheShip:"Do not search the ship."}},me={title:"Epilogue",epilogue1:"<p>Despite all odds, humanity survived the second apocalypse. Beneath the light of new stars and amidst the dust of the dead, humanity enters a golden era of scientific development and prosperity. When the white dwarf that used to be the sun extinguishes, mankind will have colonized half a galaxy worth of stars. Some of the worlds will succumb to the madness of the Ancient Ones, but most will survive — and thrive. And yet, after billions and billions of years, the net entropy of the universe continues to increase, slowly and steadily. The stars go dim, one by one, until what the beings that descended from what was once humanity must survive by extracting the negligible amount of radiation released by the only celestial bodies remaining in the universe – black holes. And still, after a finite but uncountable time, even the black holes will evaporate…</p>",epilogue2:"<p>Humanity may have perished along with its star, but not all life in the universe is aligned with the Ancients Ones. The fungoid Mi-Go scientists escaped the solar system with the infinite trove of knowledge they collected from observing the humans. The descendants of the Mi-Go would live on, and colonize many galaxies in search of more knowledge to satisfy their ravenous curiosity. And yet, after billions and billions of years, the net entropy of the universe continues to increase, slowly and steadily. The stars go dim, one by one, until what the beings that descended from what was once the Mi-Go must survive by extracting the negligible amount of radiation released by the only celestial bodies remaining in the universe – black holes. And still, after a finite but uncountable time, even the black holes will evaporate…</p>",epilogue3:"<p>And when all the black holes do disappear, and all that is left is a vacuum of vastly separated photons and electrons, life in the cosmos will cease to exist. Our universe succumbs to a cold and empty death, leaving behind a world of maximum decay and infinite dark matter – A world that was once known to some as Carcosa.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the realm of Carcosa overtook our universe, and Tassilda rules over the black stars</i>.</li></ul>",epilogue4:"<p>But humanity is not alone. They have encountered countless alien species throughout the universe and shared their knowledge and advancements towards finding a way to reverse entropy. The final piece of the puzzle was information that had been collected by the Mi-Go scientists of Yuggoth – the data within six human brains that once populated a kindergarten class on Earth, before the Ancient Ones first awakened. And thus, with the essential help of the Mi-Go, the Royal Family of Carcosa was imprisoned in their mad realm of Carcosa once more, and yellow stars rise again in the rebirth of a brighter universe.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>Hastur and Tassilda are imprisoned in Carcosa once more, and the universe vanquished the inevitable… For now</i>.</li></ul>"},dt={interludes:he,headings:le,missionBriefing:de,heirToCarcosa:ce,theSearchForFragment:ue,introspection:pe,epilogue:me},ct=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:dt,epilogue:me,headings:le,heirToCarcosa:ce,interludes:he,introspection:pe,missionBriefing:de,theSearchForFragment:ue},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),ye={resolutions:{noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"<p class='basic'>_If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated), and an investigator resigned with the Erwin Simmons story asset under their control:_ Proceed to _Resolution 3_.</p><p class='basic'>_If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated), and the investigators did not resign with the Erwin Simmons story asset under their control:_ Proceed to _Resolution 1_.</p>"},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p>_Resolution 1:_ When you finally came back to your senses, you and your companions were inside the Tatterdemalion, and Elbrus appears to have disappeared—possibly lost in space and time within the quantum realm. You don’t remember much of what happened. Despite the initial evidence pointing to the contrary—proof was eventually found that the ordeal has been real—shards of the quantum-behaving crystals were discovered in the cargo bay, that you presumably have brought back from Elbrus. Still unsure of why the cultists have come, you prepare for the next destination, which may finally give a few answers rather than pose more questions.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that *the Elbrus Station has been lost in the quantum realm*.</li><li>If it is not already written, record in your Campaign Log that *you have witnessed the primordial chaos*.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li>_Experience_: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 4 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Return to _The Search for Fragment_.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p>_Resolution 2:_ The physicist is more than grateful for your help. “All this vital research—thank god you came in time. If you ever need to get something done in the Colonial territories, I’ll make sure to put in my good word.” With a nod and an awkward handshake, you depart the facility and return to the Tatterdemalion. The cultists have stolen the quantum shards from Elbrus, but for what purpose, you are still unsure.</p><p>You look into the ephemeral glow of the crystal shard Erwin has gifted you, wondering about the bizarre circumstances you have found yourself in. However, there’s no time to waste on self-reflection—K2-PS187 awaits your next heading.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that *the Elbrus Station has been fully stabilized*.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li>_Experience_: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign for catching the eye of the King in Yellow.</li><li>Add 1 tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Return to _The Search for Fragment_.</li></ul>"},resolution3:{title:"Resolution 3",body:"<p>_Resolution 3:_ A few moments after you return to the Tatterdemalion, Elbrus implodes in a cacophony of ephemeral haze and pops out of existence. The physicist sighs in relief. “Thank god you came in time. It’s a shame about all that research that was lost, but at least everyone is safe. Now please explain to me why we are now in the very ship I remember came to pillage our facility.” You brief Erwin on your quest and discuss what purposes the cultists could have had with the quantum shards. The physicist proposes several ideas of quantum weaponry or tools—but none of which makes any sense. Regardless, he is willing to join you on your quest—out of good will or curiosity, you are unsure. Still unsure of why the cultists have come, you prepare for the next destination, which may finally give a few answers rather than pose more questions.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that *the Elbrus Station has been lost in the quantum realm*.</li><li>An investigator may add the Erwin Simmons *(Quantum Physicist)* story asset to their deck. This card does not count toward that investigator’s deck limit.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li>_Experience_: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 2 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Return to _The Search for Fragment_.</li></ul>"}},intro:{title:"Scenario IIIa: Lost Quantum",body:"<p>“When the world ended, the various scientific and mining communities of different nationalities that lie in the asteroid belt between the planets Mars and Jupiter had formed a pact—a promise to ensure the survival of mankind. [...] The United Colonial Coalition is composed of twenty colonies, varying widely in size, population, and purpose. Some colonies exist solely for mining, while others focus on scientific research or are engineering centers; these usually have fewer than 200 individuals living within them. Other asteroids serve as population centers, containing vast hydroponic farms, universities, and recreational areas. These can be home to more than a thousand colonists...”</p><p class='basic right'>— Maja, Information Archives</p><p>When you arrive at the asteroid, you are absorbed by the fuchsia glow of Elbrus. Quantum materials have only recently been discovered, but may hold key properties that could be used to engineer devices that would have been impossible with classical materials. Unfortunately, quantum fields generated by these materials disrupt traditional radio communication, making it impossible for you to hail the scientists on Elbrus. Without further ado, you and your companions board one of the landing crafts and drift towards the asteroid...</p><p>The purple aurora spreads over the view port like distant milk, filling the room with an electric tinge. Your final approach vector takes you directly over one of the larger craters on the asteroid. The computer calculates the trajectories, and commences the final descent onto the rocky surface. It is just then that the short-range radios crackle into a man’s terrified voice. “Abort the landing procedure now! Abort! Before—” But it is too late. The warning lights begin flashing on and off as the craft spins out of control. You grab onto anything you can, but the vessel increasingly spins and spins until your arms flail and darkness prevails...</p>"},setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Lost Quantum</i> and <i>Deep Space</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/lost-quantum.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/deep-space.png' /></section>",setAsideErwinSimmons:"Set aside both copies of the Erwin Simmons story asset, out of play.",setAsideFeasterFromAfar:"Set aside The Feaster from Afar enemy (with a scanning back).",createScanningDeck:"Create the scanning deck. This is done by taking all the other encounter cards with icons at the bottom of their back side and shuffling them together.",placeLandingCraft:"Search the scanning deck for the Landing Craft location and put it into play.",startAt:"Each investigator begins play at the Landing Craft.",randomizeAgenda:"Randomly shuffle the 3 versions of agenda 1 together to form the agenda deck."},tokens:{easyStandard:{skull:"-X. X is the number of face-down encounter cards in your threat area.",cultist:"-X. X is half the number of locations in play (rounded down).",tablet:"-1. Reveal another token. If you fail, put the top card of the encounter deck into your threat area, face-down.",elderThing:"-3. Randomly draw a face-down encounter card in your threat area."},hardExpert:{skull:"-X. X is the number of face-down encounter cards in your threat area.",cultist:"-X. X is the number of locations in play.",tablet:"-2. Reveal another token. If you fail, put the top card of the encounter deck into your threat area, face-down.",elderThing:"-4. Randomly draw a face-down encounter card in your threat area."}},specialRules:[{title:"Face-Down Encounter Cards",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, you may be instructed to place encounter cards face-down into your threat area. These cards are considered out-of-play, but may be referenced by other scenario cards.</p><p class='basic'>When you would draw cards from the encounter deck, if both the encounter deck and discard piles are empty, draw a card from the face-down encounter cards in your threat area instead. If there are none in your threat area, you are defeated.</p>"},{title:"Clues & Locations in the Quantum Realm",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, locations may leave play and re-enter play at a later time. When a location leaves play, discard all attached cards and clues on it. When a location enters play, regardless of if it has been in play at a previous time, treat it as if you have just revealed it for the first time. As such, a number of clues equal to that location’s clue value are placed on that location each time it is revealed (from the token pool).</p>"}]},ut={lostQuantum:ye},pt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:ut,lostQuantum:ye},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),ge=JSON.parse(`{"intro":{"title":"Scenario VI: Starfall","body":"<p>It is beyond doubt. The sun is experiencing an unprecedented acceleration in the decay of its hydrogen core. K2-PS187 estimates that there are only a few years left before the fusion reactions that fuel our star will run out of gas and collapse on itself, generating a radioactive supernova that will destroy all life within a few light years. Whatever the cultists have done within Fragment has doomed our solar system to a premature end.</p><p>Your only hope now is to convince the remainder of the various colonies of humanity of this accelerated death and help them gather the resources and technology necessary to survive the supernova in any way possible. K2-PS187 makes the preparations for the navigation console as you brace for the many-months long journey ahead of you travelling across the solar system to save humanity.</p>","proceedToAnotherPath":"Check your Campaign Log. If the investigators <i>know of the Abjuration of the Throne</i>, proceed to <b>Another Path</b>.","skipToSetup":"Otherwise, skip to <b>Setup</b>."},"anotherPath":{"title":"Another Path","body":"<p>Perhaps there is another way. The ritual you've glimpsed in the halls of Tassilda's temple will take many months to prepare—and you still do not know where it must be performed, but if it is possible, it will surely give humanity enough time to develop the technology necessary to survive. Now to find the ritual site is another question altogether…</p><ul><li>Proceed to <b>Setup</b>.</li></ul>"},"setup":{"gatherSets":"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Starfall</i>, <i>Anachronism</i>, <i>Deep Space</i>, <i>Endtimes</i>, and <i>Agents of Yog-Sothoth</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/starfall.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/anachronism.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/deep-space.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/endtimes.png' /><img src='{setImgPath}/agents-of-yog.png' /></section>","setAsideHastursGaze":"Set aside the <i>Hastur's Gaze</i> encounter set. This set is indicated by the following icon:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/hasturs-gaze.png' /></section>","setAsideCards":"Set the following cards aside, out of play: the The Cassilda location, the Domaag T'eel enemy, the Mi-Go Sentinel enemy, the Yithian Guard enemy, and The Feaster from Afar.","setAsideAgenda":"Set aside the Dark Matter agenda and Tassilda's Awakening act, as well as the Tassilda enemy, out of play.","checkCampaignLog":"Check your Campaign Log:","elbrusStation":"If <i>Elbrus Station has been fully stabilized</i>, set aside the Ar-NO story asset, out of play. Otherwise, set aside the Project Origami story asset, out of play.","nostalgiaII":"If <i>the Nostalgia II has been saved</i>, set aside the Director Cixin story asset, out of play. Otherwise, set aside the Last Hope story asset, out of play.","miGoAlliance":"If <i>you are allied with the Mi-Go</i>, set aside the Mi-Go Collector story asset, out of play. Otherwise, set aside the Repairing the Threshold story asset, out of play.","createScanningDeck":"Create the scanning deck. This is done by taking all the other encounter cards with icons at the bottom of their back side and shuffling them together. (Including the cards above that have not been set aside.)","placeLocations":"Put the following locations into play: The Tatterdemalion, Mars, Asteroid Belt and Pluto.","startAt":"Each investigator begins play at The Tatterdemalion.","impendingDoom":"For every tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log, begin the scenario with 1 additional doom on the agenda."},"tokens":{"easyStandard":{"skull":"-X. X is half the number of revealed locations without clues (rounded up).","cultist":"-3. If you fail by 2 or more, take 1 damage and 1 horror.","tablet":"Increase the difficulty of this skill test by 1. Reveal another token.","elderThing":"-3. If you fail, you must either place 1 doom on the current agenda, or take 1 horror for each point you fail by."},"hardExpert":{"skull":"-X. X is half the number of locations in play (rounded up).","cultist":"-4. If you fail by 2 or more, take 1 damage and 1 horror.","tablet":"Increase the difficulty of this skill test by 1. Reveal another token.","elderThing":"-4. If you fail, you must either place 1 doom on the current agenda, or take 1 horror for each point you fail by."}},"resolutions":{"noResolution":{"title":"No Resolution Was Reached","body":"<p><b>If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated):</b> Proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.</p>"},"resolution1":{"title":"Resolution 1","body":"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> A brilliant light shines over the solar system. The cataclysmic supernova radiates through the void, annihilating all unprotected life and stripping all the heavenly bodies of their precious atmosphere, leaving barren worlds in its wake.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the sun went supernova and wiped out most of the solar system</i>.</li><li>If Repairing the Threshold is in the victory display, in your Campaign Log, record that <i>Mi-Go safely returned to their home world</i>.</li><li>If Last Hope is in the victory display, in your Campaign Log, record that <i>Hope was shielded from the blast</i>. The investigators who resigned in Hope read <b>Beyond Hope</b>.</li><li>If Project Origami is in the victory display, in your Campaign Log, record that <i>The UCC escaped to another galaxy</i>. The investigators who resigned in New Brooklyn read <b>Far, Far Away</b>.</li><li>If none of the story cards mentioned above are in the victory display, the remaining investigators must read <b>The End 1</b>. Otherwise, they read <b>The End 2</b>.</li></ul>"},"resolution2":{"title":"Resolution 2","body":"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> The Royal Princess of Carcosa succumbs to your assault and wastes away before you. You have defeated Tassilda, and in doing so have prevented the early collapse of the sun. Suddenly there is a horrific smell wafting down all around you, carried by a blast of chilly air. Before any of you can react, a dark cloud crackling with arcs of yellow and white energy expels from the sun, surrounding the entire ship. Within this cloud hovers a horrific creature. It is enormous, wrinkled, and hunched, with dozens of tentacles, each tipped with a wicked-looking fang. This can only be the being Tassilda spoke of, her sire, the Last King. In an instant, the great abomination begins crushing the hull of the ship inwards. In your final moments, despite being unable to save yourself from the blast, you feel accomplished—and redeemed—by what you have done to save the others.</p><ul><li>Proceed to <b>The End 3</b>.</li></ul>"}},"beyondHope":{"title":"Beyond Hope","body":"<p>After the blackout finally ended, you and your fellow companions left the underground shelters of Hope to witness a dazzling array of painterly gases, and a faint white sphere—the residual legacy of the sun. Colony researchers have claimed that it would have been impossible for the electromagnetic shield to protect the entire planet from the blast without the unexpected but embraced energy spike originating from the nearby alien ruins. It is the dawn of a new beginning for mankind, the age of the White Sun. You live the rest of your days helping the megapolis sustain itself and recounting the fantasy stories of your life on Earth. And yet you wonder, as you look up to the light of the white dwarf, how long until it too, inevitably decays and humanity will once more need to escape extinction…</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that your investigator <i>lived the remainder of their days, with Hope</i>.</li><li>The investigators win the campaign!</li><li>Proceed to the <b>Epilogue</b>.</li></ul>"},"farFarAway":{"title":"Far, Far Away","body":"<p>The scientists of Sinai activated the space-time warping device moments before the blast. The colony of New Brooklyn was jaunted along the folds of space time, towards a new galaxy, and a new future. The destination—a prospective binary system of many exoplanets—appears to be safe and far beyond the reach of the Ancient Ones of the old world. You live the rest of your days helping humanity build outposts under the virgin skies of a new home, a planet the settlers will call Paradise. You recount stories of your life on Earth to your descendants, stories that will become fairy tales and eventually legends. The inhabitants upon this new world live and work together in peace and prosperity. It is the dawn of a new beginning for mankind. And yet you wonder, as you look up to the light of your new stars, how long until they too, inevitably decay and humanity will once more need to escape extinction…</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that your investigator <i>lived the remainder of their days, on Paradise</i>.</li><li>The investigators win the campaign!</li><li>Proceed to the <b>Epilogue</b>.</li></ul>"},"theEnd1":{"title":"The End 1","body":"<p>The light of the supernova engulfs the skies and surrounds you and your companions. Despite all of your efforts, you could not redeem yourself and prevent the demise of humanity. In your finals moments, before the shockwave strips you of your corporeal essence, a figure in a tattered yellow dress materializes in the light. You kneel before her and grab onto her hand, as Tassilda welcomes you into the dark realm of Carcosa.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you have returned to the palaces of Dim Carcosa</i>.</li><li>Each investigator is <b>killed</b>.</li><li>The investigators lose the campaign.</li></ul>"},"theEnd2":{"title":"The End 2","body":"<p>The light of the supernova engulfs the skies and surrounds you and your companions. Despite being unable to save yourself from the blast, you still feel accomplished—and redeemed—by what you have done to save others. In your finals moments, before the shockwave strips you of your corporeal essence, you shut your eyes in acceptance of your terrible fate.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that your investigator <i>was caught in the supernova's blast</i>.</li><li>Each investigator is <b>killed</b>.</li><li>If all investigators are reading this, the investigators lose the campaign.</li><li>Proceed to the <b>Epilogue</b>.</li></ul>"},"theEnd3":{"title":"The End 3","body":"<p>A roar of applause startles you awake. The crowd of the theatre rises to their feet, cheering endlessly. Several patrons in the front row are throwing roses to the actors on stage, who are bowing with wide smiles across their faces. A searing headache crawls through your temples. How did you get back here? Were you in the theatre all along? What about the Tatterdemalion? K2-PS187? Fragment? …the entire future? Was it all just a terrible dream? You exit the auditorium before the crowd rushes to do the same. Dizziness and exhaustion harries your senses. The weight of your lengthy adventure is crushing your mind. By the time you finally reach the lobby, you are clawing your way across the ground. The ground… Earth. You are finally home. A few of your thoughts wander towards the idea that this might be another simulation or a trick of the mind, but you don't care anymore. You can live with that. At least now, there is hope for a brighter future.</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>the investigators have finally escaped Hastur's grasp and prevented him from escaping his prison</i>.</li><li>The investigators win the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Each investigator may heal up to 2 mental trauma, as they now have hope.</li><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>Hope was shielded from the blast</i>, <i>the UCC escaped to another galaxy</i> and <i>the Mi-Go safely returned to their home world</i>.</li><li>Proceed to the <b>Epilogue</b>.</li></ul>"}}`),mt={starfall:ge},yt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:mt,starfall:ge},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),fe={intro:{title:"Scenario IIIc: Strange Moons",body:"<p>“Humanity’s first contact with the extraterrestrials was in the early 21st century, when a lunar expedition stumbled upon a vast underground network of alien structures underneath the sea of regolith. The Greys, as humanity has come to know them, were under the guise of a curious species that came to our solar system to observe and probe the young civilization. The true purpose of their lunar activities have remained concealed for many years…”</p><p class='basic right'>— Maja, Information Archives</p><p>You look out the view ports and can see only dense, orange clouds for most of the descent. Only after the landing shuttle dipped into the troposphere that the clouds are thin enough for you to peer at the ground below — miles and miles of windswept dunes of methane snow, broken by knife-like volcanic ridges of icy stone, open craters belching “lava flows” of liquid water, ammonia, and methane that freeze into fantastic shapes as they pour down the slopes. You could never have dreamed of anything like the beauty and alien landscape of Titan.</p><p>The craft lands smoothly onto a flat slab of ice. After K2-PS187 confirms that this is the coordinates of the unusual “business trips” that the cultists were conducting, you suit up, open the hatch and step out into the harsh terrain. A large tunnel nestled between the orange cliffs greets you. A green glow pulsates from within, illuminating a strange figure, guarding the entrance…</p>"},setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Strange Moons</i> and <i>Deep Space</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/strange-moons.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/deep-space.png' /></section>",setAsideInterstellarPredators:"Set aside the <i>Interstellar Predators</i> encounter set, out of play. This set is indicated by the following icon:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/interstellar-predators.png' /></section>",setAsideBrains:"Set aside each *Brain* story asset, out of play.",setAsideFeasterFromAfar:"Set aside The Feaster from Afar enemy (with a scanning back).",createScanningDeck:"Create the scanning deck. This is done by taking all the other encounter cards with icons at the bottom of their back side and shuffling them together.",placeLocations:"Put all remaining locations into play.",startAt:"Each investigator begins play at the Entrance Tunnel.",spawnTheGreys:"Spawn the The Greys enemy at the Entrance Tunnel."},tokens:{easyStandard:{skull:"-2. If you fail, deal 1 damage to a *Brain* story asset.",cultist:"-2. If you revealed another chaos token during this test, take 1 horror.",tablet:"Reveal 2 additional tokens for this test.",elderThing:"-3. If this is an attack or evasion attempt against a *Byakhee* enemy, reveal an additional token for this test."},hardExpert:{skull:"-3. If you fail, deal 1 damage to the nearest *Brain* story asset.",cultist:"-3. If you revealed another chaos token during this test, take 1 horror.",tablet:"Reveal 2 additional tokens for this test.",elderThing:"-4. If this is an attack or evasion attempt against a *Byakhee* enemy, reveal an additional token for this test."}},specialRules:[{title:"Seal",body:"<p class='basic'>Some cards may have the ability to seal one or more chaos tokens as part of their effect. This is done as follows: Search the chaos bag for the specified token, remove it from the chaos bag, and place it on the card. If the specified token is not in the chaos bag, the effect fails.</p><p class='basic'>When a chaos token is “released,” it is returned to the chaos bag and is no longer considered sealed. <b>If a card with one or more chaos tokens sealed on it leaves play for any reason, any chaos tokens sealed on it are immediately released.</b></p>"},{title:"Patrol",body:"<p class='basic'>Some enemies have the patrol keyword. During the enemy phase (in framework step 3.2), each ready, unengaged enemy with the patrol keyword moves to a connecting location along the shortest path toward the designated location (as described in parentheses next to the word patrol).</p><ul><li>If there are multiple locations that qualify as the designated location, the lead investigator may choose which location the enemy moves toward.</li><li>If an enemy with patrol would be compelled to move to a location which is blocked by a card ability, the enemy does not move.</li></ul>"},{title:"Brain Scanning",body:"<p class='basic'>In this scenario, <b>Scan</b> abilities will instruct you to search the scanning deck for a card with two matching icons. A card that contains only one of the two icons is invalid, and cannot be chosen for the scan. The card in the scanning deck must contain both of the indicated icons, in any order.</p>"},{title:"Combined Skill Tests",body:"<p class='basic'>Some skill tests in this scenario will require investigators to test multiple skills at once. To perform such a skill test, simply add both indicated skills and reveal and resolve a chaos token, compare the modified skill value to the difficulty of the test. Such a test is considered to be a test of both skill types. Cards with either skill icon may be committed to the test, and both icons are considered matching skill icons. <i>(Skill icons only contribute once for skill tests that involve additions of the same skill.)</i></p>"},{title:"Replacing Locations",body:"<p class='basic'>Throughout this scenario, you may be instructed to place new locations on top of existing ones. When a location is placed on top of a location that is already in play, it takes its place. All tokens, attachments, investigators, enemies, and other cards at the former location are considered to now be at the new location (they have not “moved”—the location simply changed). If a location leaves play and there is another location underneath it, that location takes its place. All tokens, attachments, investigators, enemies, and other cards at the location leaving play are considered to now be at the former location.</p>"}],resolutions:{xp:{resolution1:"Further understanding of the agents of the King in Yellow"},noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"<p><b>If no resolution was reached:</b></p><ul><li>If at least 1 investigator resigned, proceed to <b>Resolution 2</b>.</li><li>If each investigator was defeated, proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> Flapping and screeching, you had no chance against the extraterrestrial swarm that descended onto Titan shortly after you have arrived. Fortunately — it seems as though you were not their target. The alien facility has been ransacked and any clues you could have gleaned have been destroyed. At the very least, they left you alone. When the coast is finally clear of the flying monstrosities, you search through the ruins to find several golden disks of various radii. Aboard the Tatterdemalion, you fiddle with these disks and try to combine them in various orientations — but they don’t appear to have any use other than the value of the material itself. There is still much you don’t know, and with resolve, you prepare for the next expedition.</p><ul><li>Record in your Campaign Log that <i>you are not in good standing with the Mi-Go</i>.</li><li>If there are 3 story cards in the victory display, record in your Campaign Log that <i>you have uncovered the cultist’s inhuman methods</i>. Then, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign for catching the eye of the King in Yellow.</li><li>Add 1 tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log, and 1 additional tally mark for each Brain story asset in play.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display. Each investigator earns 2 additional experience as they gain further understanding of the agents of the King in Yellow.<ul><li><b>Experience</b>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Return to <b>The Search for Fragment</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> On board the Tatterdemalion, you try to decipher the meaning of the various glimpses you’ve seen within the alien facility, but nothing strikes you as particularly significant. A thorough search of the cargo hold reveals a stack of the golden disks that were exchanged during the transaction. You fiddle with them and try to combine them in various orientations — but they don’t appear to have any use other than the value of the material itself. There is still much you don’t know, and with resolve, you prepare for the next expedition.</p><ul><li>If there are 3 story cards in the victory display, record in your Campaign Log that <i>you have uncovered the cultist’s inhuman methods</i>. Then, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign for catching the eye of the King in Yellow.</li><li>If a copy of Mi-Go Scientist is in the victory display, record in your Campaign Log that <i>you are not in good standing with the Mi-Go</i>. Otherwise, record that <i>you are allied with the Mi-Go</i>.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><b>Experience</b>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 1 tally mark under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Return to <b>The Search for Fragment</b>.</li></ul>"}}},gt={strangeMoons:fe},ft=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:gt,strangeMoons:fe},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),be={theManInThePallidMask:{label:{gainClueAndHeal:"Gain 1 clue from the token bank and heal up to 2 damage and 2 horror",addMemory:"Add 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”"}},intro:{title:"Scenario IV: The Machine in Yellow",body:"<p>You awaken with a start, as though shaken by an unseen force. There are only a few other patrons in the audience, and no performers on stage. The lights are dimmed, and the stage curtains are tattered and ripped. A foul but unrecognizable smell permeates the air. You are back in the Ward theatre — where it all began. Is this an artifact of your memory? Or have you been dreaming this entire time? Shaking off your drowsiness, you call out into the air for K2-PS187. To your relief, and slight disappointment, the digitalized voices respond in confirmation that the procedure behaved as planned. You have arrived inside of your own mind…</p>"},setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>Curtain Call</i>, <i>The Machine in Yellow</i>, <i>Dark Past</i>, <i>Delusions</i> and <i>Rats</i>. <i>(Curtain Call and Delusions are from The Path to Carcosa.)</i> These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{setImgPath}/curtain-call.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/the-machine-in-yellow.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/dark-past.png' /><img src='{setImgPath}/delusions.png' /><img src='{setImgPath}/rats.png' /></section>When gathering the <i>Curtain Call</i> encounter set, only gather the locations.",maddeningDelusions:"The investigators may choose to use the <i>Maddening Delusions</i> encounter set (from Return to The Path to Carcosa) instead of the <i>Delusions</i> encounter set. If you do so, each investigator may add 1 tally mark next to their “Memories”. This set is indicated by the following icon:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{setImgPath}/maddening-delusions.png' /></section>",placeLocations:"Put the Theatre, Lobby, Balcony, and Backstage locations into play.",startAt:"Each investigator begins play at the Theatre.",setAsideDoorways:"Set aside each copy of the Backstage Doorway and Lobby Doorway locations, out of play.",setAsideYourOtherSelf:"Set aside each copy of the Your Other Self enemy, out of play."},maddeningDelusions:{label:{useMaddeningDelusions:"Use the <i>Maddening Delusions</i> encounter set",useDelusions:"Use the <i>Delusions</i> encounter set",addMemory:"Add 1 tally mark next to your “Memories”",doNotAddMemory:"Do not add a tally mark"}},tokens:{easyStandard:{skull:"-X. X is half of your “Memories” (rounded down).",cultist:"-X. X is the number of hidden cards in your hand.",tablet:"Reveal another token. Double that token's modifier.",elderThing:"-4. You may choose to cross out a tally mark next to your investigator's “Memories” to automatically succeed."},hardExpert:{skull:"-X. X is your “Memories”.",cultist:"-X. X is the number of hidden cards in your hand.",tablet:"Reveal another token. Double that token's modifier.",elderThing:"-6. You may choose to cross out a tally mark next to your investigator's “Memories” to automatically succeed."}},resolutions:{xp:{resolution1:"Reliving their past memories"},noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"<p><b>If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated):</b> Proceed to <b>Resolution 1</b>.</p>"},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> You had a dream. A vivid, lucid and all-too real dream. You escaped the Ward theatre into the rainy streets of Arkham. You would visit the after-party of the dreadful <i>King in Yellow</i>, and embark along a grand and mind-bending adventure across Arkham which eventually leads to France and into Carcosa itself. When you finally wake up in cold sweat back in the cryo-chamber, you almost forgot the new reality you had found yourself in. Although the ordeal has been difficult and took much longer than you anticipated, you have finally unlocked that part of your memories that has been kept concealed by your other self—the ritual to locate the Fragment of Carcosa.</p><ul><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display. Each investigator earns 2 additional experience for reliving their past memories.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Add 2 tally marks under “Impending Doom” in your Campaign Log.</li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario V: Fragment of Carcosa</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution2:{title:"Resolution 2",body:"<p><b>Resolution 2:</b> With the infectious tumor that is the cultist’s consciousness finally ejected from your mind, you have unlocked that part of your memories that has been kept concealed by your other self—the ritual to locate the Fragment of Carcosa. Without further ado, you quickly disconnect yourself from the virtual dreamlands and return to form in the Tatterdemalion, ready to confront Tassilda at long last.</p><ul><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario V: Fragment of Carcosa</b>.</li></ul>"}}},bt={theMachineInYellow:be},wt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:bt,theMachineInYellow:be},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),we={setup:{gatherSets:"Gather all cards from the following encounter sets: <i>The Tatterdemalion</i>, <i>Anachronism</i>, and <i>Dark Past</i>. These sets are indicated by the following icons:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/the-tatterdemalion.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/anachronism.png' /><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/dark-past.png' /></section>",setAsideArtificialIntelligence:"Set aside the <i>Artificial Intelligence</i> encounter set, out of play. This set is indicated by the following icon:<section class='encounter-sets'><img src='{imgPath}/homebrew/dark-matter/sets/artificial-intelligence.png' /></section>",setAsideVirtualAccessKey:"Set aside the Virtual Access Key story asset, out of play.",scanningDeck:"Create the scanning deck. This is done by taking all the encounter cards with icons at the bottom of their back side and shuffling them together.",placeLocations:"Put all remaining locations into play.",startAt:"Each investigator begins play at the Cryosleep Quarters."},resolutions:{noResolution:{title:"No Resolution Was Reached",body:"<p><b>If no resolution was reached (each investigator resigned or was defeated):</b> Once again you are startled awake, this time by the small, cold hands of a young girl. “It worked! You’re here! Please, follow me quickly.” You are surprised to find yourself standing in a field of grass. The sky is black and seething, the sun unable to penetrate the dark, rolling storm clouds… You are no longer on the Tatterdemalion, but you don’t recognize this place either. Metallic cylinders with red, pulsating lights stand tall in the distance, looming above a small town. Behind you is a large obsidian door.</p><p>You ask the little girl about your whereabouts. “You are in a simulated dream. In fact, you are in <i>my</i> dream. Now follow me quickly before the monster eats my friends.”</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you were transported to the Virtual Dreamlands by Maja</i>.</li><li>If an investigator was defeated or resigned with Cybervirus in their hand, that investigator must record in the Campaign Log that they <i>have been infected by the cybervirus</i>.</li><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario II: Electric Nightmare</b>.</li></ul>"},resolution1:{title:"Resolution 1",body:"<p><b>Resolution 1:</b> You find yourself standing in a field of grass. You are no longer on the Tatterdemalion, but you don’t recognize this place either. The sky is black and seething, the sun unable to penetrate the dark, rolling storm clouds. Metallic cylinders with red, pulsating lights stand tall in the distance, looming above a small town.</p><p>This system’s pocket dream reality is like nothing you have ever experienced. The colors, textures, sounds, and scents are startlingly realistic. Behind you is a large obsidian door, a virtual gateway to represent your arrival.</p><p>You are surprised to see a little girl walking towards you. “You got here just in time! Please, follow me quickly before the monster eats my friends.”</p><ul><li>In your Campaign Log, record that <i>you entered the Virtual Dreamlands by your own means</i>.</li><li>If an investigator was defeated, resigned, or ended their game with Cybervirus in their hand, that investigator must record in the Campaign Log that they <i>have been infected by the cybervirus</i>.</li><li>If at least 1 copy of the Reminiscence treachery is in the victory display, add 1 {'{'}elderThing{'}'} token to the chaos bag for the remainder of the campaign.</li><li>Each investigator earns experience equal to the Victory X value of each card in the victory display.<ul><li><i>Experience</i>: {xp}</li></ul></li><li>Proceed to <b>Scenario II: Electric Nightmare</b>.</li></ul>"}}},vt={theTatterdemalion:we},kt=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:vt,theTatterdemalion:we},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),ve="暗物质",ke={title:"在太空，没有人能听见你的尖叫",body:"<p class='basic'>“他提到卡尔克萨王朝的创建，连接哈斯塔、毕宿五与昴宿星团之谜的湖泊；又谈到卡西尔达、卡蜜拉，以及德姆赫与哈利湖的幽暗深处。”</p><p class='basic right'>- 罗伯特·W·钱伯斯，《名誉修复者》</p><p>2147年，你从一艘仿佛被遗弃的太空船的冷冻休眠中醒来，随即踏上横越太阳系的深空冒险，试图阻止人类灭绝。《暗物质》由 Axolotl 设计，是一套供1-4名玩家游玩、包含8场冒险的《诡镇奇谈：卡牌版》爱好者剧本，灵感来自《克苏鲁的呼唤》补充资料《卡尔克萨的涟漪》与《终末时刻》。本剧本需要《卡尔克萨之路》豪华扩展；建议先完成《卡尔克萨之路》再游玩，以获得最佳体验。</p>"},Te=[{title:"扫描",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.scan"},{title:"记忆",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.memories"},{title:"警戒",body:"@:darkMatter.additionalRulesAndClarifications.alert"}],Ie={title:"附加规则与说明",scan:"<h3>扫描</h3><p class='basic'>本剧本部分遭遇卡背面底部印有图示。这些卡会组成“扫描牌堆”，即在某些冒险设置时创建、位于游戏外的牌堆。</p><p class='basic'>带有<b>扫描</b>行动标识的能力让调查员探索环境，通常用来从扫描牌堆中寻找推进冒险所需的剧情支援、剧情卡或地点；通常但不总是通过“启动”行动发动。</p><p class='basic'><b>扫描</b>能力会要求你寻找扫描牌堆顶牌上带有指定图示的卡。查看顶牌底部图示；<b>若其图示与所扫描的图示相同，抽取该卡。</b>这视为“成功”扫描。若未抽取任何卡，则扫描“失败”。</p><p class='basic'>若顶牌没有匹配图示，将其背面朝下置于扫描牌堆旁，继续检查下一张，直到抽到指定类型的卡。此行动结束后，将置于扫描牌堆旁的所有卡洗回扫描牌堆。</p><p class='basic'><b>扫描</b>能力通常会提及地点图示；地点图示即卡牌左上角的连接符号。若需弃掉带有扫描背面的卡，或将其洗入任何其他牌堆，则改为将其洗回扫描牌堆。</p>",memories:"<h3>记忆</h3><p class='basic'>部分冒险卡、剧情结局与幕间会提及你的“记忆”。每位调查员在剧本日志中都有独立的“记忆”栏位。<b>记忆只属于对应调查员，不与其他调查员共享。</b></p><p class='basic'>若指示你在某位调查员的“记忆”旁增加或划掉计数，便在其剧本日志的对应栏位添加或划掉一条。该调查员未被划掉的计数数量即为其“记忆”数量。</p>",alert:"<h3>警戒</h3><p class='basic'>调查员尝试躲避带有警戒关键词的敌人时，若技能检定失败，在结算该检定全部结果后，该敌人对该调查员进行一次攻击。敌人进行警戒攻击后不会横置；无论该敌人是否与该调查员交战，都会进行此攻击。</p>"},Se={title:"序幕",body:"<p>你翻开手中折起的节目单，再次阅读仿佛你已读过百遍的这张纸片。“米斯卡塔尼克剧院上演：《黄衣之王》，”纸上这么写着。“阿卡姆本地的沃德剧院将迎来这部戏剧的特别上演，为期一晚。这部令人无法抗拒的戏剧共有两幕。本作品由奈杰尔·英格兰姆负责筹划和管理。本剧演员均属于一个小型剧团，在演员名单最后还有个未署名的人物：‘陌生人。’”</p><p>这样一部万众期待的戏剧不远万里从巴黎来到阿卡姆，即便只上演一夜，它也备受瞩目。在演出前的几个星期里，它一直是城中热话。虽然迹象不甚明显……然而，你有证据证明有某种邪恶势力正在行动。最初是剧院有个舞台工作人员失踪，一个才十七岁的男孩在一次彩排中缺席，之后就再也没人见过他。到距离演出已不到两个星期的时候，一位音乐家被发现死亡，并且尸体口中含着枪。或许最让人生畏的是警察从独立广场抓到的疯汉，他满口胡言乱语，说着“王已归来”之类的疯话。他被带到阿卡姆疯人院之后，你惊讶地发现，产生这种妄想的并不止他一人。</p><p>你和同伴深入调查后，发现这些事件十分可疑。尽管无法证实它们之间有何关联，这部即将上演的戏剧周围所发生的离奇事件却远不止这些。一桩桩自杀与发疯事件接踵而来，你决心找出背后的真相。</p><p>观众席的灯光暗了下来，聚光灯落在舞台上。眼前的情景与你的预期相去甚远。《黄衣之王》的第一幕缓慢而单调，使人感到无聊乏味。这部戏剧的背景和角色足够吸引人，但曲折而怪诞的剧情却无法娱乐观众，也传达不了什么信息。你开始怀疑这些发生在《黄衣之王》周围的骇人事件是不是根本没有联系。或许这不过是你想象过度；这场平凡而不起眼的演出怎能引起这般混乱？令你吃惊的是，第一幕没有任何高潮和转折就骤然结束了。幕间休息时灯光亮起，你忍住哈欠，想要提早离场。你正在踌躇之中，突然感觉困意越来越浓……最终昏睡了过去。</p><p class='basic right'>进入<b>冒险I：破衣号</b>。</p>"},Ce={label:{noInvestigatorAddsK2:"没有调查员将其加入自己的牌组"}},Ae={title:"失步",body:"<p>校园里，一辆翻倒的校车蒙着尘土。你在被破坏的车窗上瞥见自己的倒影，却不再认得那张脸。熟悉的身形与五官明明近在眼前，却绝非你的身体。玻璃中的面孔逐渐化作没有口鼻眼的苍白空白面具；虚拟现实已无法识别你残留的自我形象，你的数字心智投影正在消散。</p><p class='basic'>你必须将“失步”弱点加入牌组；该卡不计入牌组张数。</p>"},Re={youWereTransportedToTheVirtualDreamlandsByMaja:"你被玛雅送入虚拟幻梦境。",youEnteredTheVirtualDreamlandsByYourOwnMeans:"你自行进入了虚拟幻梦境。",hasBeenInfectedByTheCybervirus:"已感染网络病毒。",youAreTrappedInAVirtualNightmare:"你被困在虚拟噩梦中。",youPartiallyRestoredTheSanityOfK2PS187:"你部分恢复了K2-PS187的理智。",youFullyRestoredTheSanityOfK2PS187:"你完全恢复了K2-PS187的理智。",youHaveWatchedThePerformanceOfHeirToCarcosa:"你观看了《卡尔克萨的继承人》演出。",theElbrusStationHasBeenLostInTheQuantumRealm:"厄尔布鲁士站迷失于量子领域。",theElbrusStationHasBeenFullyStabilized:"厄尔布鲁士站已完全稳定。",youHaveWitnessedThePrimordialChaos:"你目睹了原初混沌。",youHaveRescuedTheRemainingCrewOfTheNostalgiaII:"你救出了怀旧II号剩余船员。",theNostalgiaIIHasBeenSaved:"怀旧II号获救。",youCouldntSaveTheCrewOfTheNostalgiaII:"你未能救下怀旧II号船员。",allInvestigatorsHaveBeenCorruptedByTheEarth:"所有调查员均被地球腐化。",youAreNotInGoodStandingWithTheMiGo:"你未获米·戈信任。",youAreAlliedWithTheMiGo:"你与米·戈结盟。",youHaveUncoveredTheCultistsInhumanMethods:"你揭露了邪教徒非人的手段。",theInvestigatorsAreTrappedWithinCarcosa:"调查员被困在卡尔克萨中。",theInvestigatorsKnowOfTheAbjurationOfTheThrone:"调查员得知了王座弃绝仪式。",theSunWentSupernovaAndWipedOutMostOfTheSolarSystem:"太阳成为超新星，摧毁了大半个太阳系。",miGoSafelyReturnedToTheirHomeWorld:"米·戈安全返回故乡。",hopeWasShieldedFromTheBlast:"希望避开了爆炸。",theUCCEscapedToAnotherGalaxy:"UCC逃往另一座星系。",livedTheRemainderOfTheirDaysWithHope:"与希望共度余生。",livedTheRemainderOfTheirDaysOnParadise:"在天堂度过余生。",youHaveReturnedToThePalacesOfDimCarcosa:"你回到了卡城幽影的宫殿。",wasCaughtInTheSupernovasBlast:"被超新星爆炸吞没。",theInvestigatorsEscapedHastursGrasp:"调查员终于逃离哈斯塔的掌控，并阻止他逃出囚牢。",theRealmOfCarcosaOvertookOurUniverse:"卡尔克萨领域吞没了我们的宇宙，塔西尔达统治着黑星。",hasturAndTassildaAreImprisonedInCarcosaOnceMore:"哈斯塔与塔西尔达再次囚禁于卡尔克萨，宇宙战胜了注定的结局……暂时如此。",impendingDoom:"迫近的毁灭",memories:"记忆"},Tt={name:ve,intro:ke,specialRules:Te,additionalRulesAndClarifications:Ie,prologue:Se,electricNightmare:Ce,desynchronization:Ae,key:Re},It=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,additionalRulesAndClarifications:Ie,default:Tt,desynchronization:Ae,electricNightmare:Ce,intro:ke,key:Re,name:ve,prologue:Se,specialRules:Te},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),_e={title:"幕间I：任务简报",missionBriefing1:"<p>环绕你的虚拟梦景化作短暂的蓝色代码旋流，随即消散在黑暗中。你回到破衣号内，机械臂从你后脑拔出网络缆线，带来一阵刺痛。K2-PS187为强行将你送入虚拟幻梦境道歉，并表示已完全合作；这台赛博超级计算机会协助你，先为你梳理破衣号近日发生的事。</p>",missionBriefing2:"<p>虚拟梦景的蓝色光流散去，你断开连接，踉跄走出熟悉的冷冻休眠舱。K2-PS187已完全合作，准备尽力帮助你；超级计算机随即开始说明破衣号近期发生的一切。</p>",missionBriefing3:"<p>破衣号的船员都是降临地球的古神哈斯塔的崇拜者。邪教徒最近执行任务，要释放据传囚于代号“碎片”的小行星上的哈斯塔之女塔西尔达。飞船与碎片会合后派出数支勘探队；在植入你现在的心智之前，你正是其中一名等待唤醒塔西尔达的邪教探险者。</p><p>数周勘探后，一队带回刻有异界象形文本的石板，命令K2-PS187翻译；另一队报告找到了塔西尔达居住的内室并毁掉囚禁符印，之后便杳无音信。你和同伴在卡尔克萨公主苏醒攻击破衣号前迅速撤离，并不为那些崇拜混沌神祇而死的同伴哀悼。任务看似成功：塔西尔达获释，或将被父亲擢升为新的古神。</p><p>多数邪教徒在返航中进入冷眠，K2-PS187却继续分析符文。翻译完成后，它读到名为《卡尔克萨的继承人》的故事，因恐惧而疯狂，屠杀所有醒着的船员；飞船从此混乱地漂流。直到最后，它从档案中把你带回世界，发出绝望求救。</p><p>你明白自己必须赎罪。尽管地球不复旧日模样，人类仍散居太阳系殖民地。若卡尔克萨继承人塔西尔达被擢升为神，她必会以卡尔克萨的疯狂统治人类。你必须在她成神前消灭她。初次腐化时，“碎片”的位置数据已遗失，但K2-PS187从航程表找回几条线索；你必须横跨太阳系，找出小行星坐标并阻止她升格。</p>",simulatedPerformance:"<p>调查员可以选择观看翻译剧本的模拟演出。</p>",label:{watchThePerformance:"观看《卡尔克萨的继承人》的模拟演出。后果自负。",declineToWatch:"不观看演出。"}},Pe={title:"卡尔克萨的继承人",body:"<p>节目开场，伊提尔王室在哈斯塔化身黄衣之王面前瑟瑟发抖。接下来的三个小时里，你目睹了一部充满背叛、阴谋与恐怖的可怕作品。故事如下：</p><p>黄衣之王占据伊提尔，将其并入卡尔克萨后，娶了发疯的卡蜜拉公主为伴侣。公主死前为这位古神生下三个孩子，他们也成了哈斯塔的养子女：两名男孩分别叫托图特和塔西洛克，女孩则叫塔西尔达。孩子们起初看似正常，后来却逐渐显出父亲的许多外貌特征与力量。母亲把这种变化视为卡尔克萨又一次腐化的结果。这最后一击彻底摧毁了卡蜜拉的神智，她的心脏也因绝望与悲痛停止了跳动。</p><p>三名王族子女曾与生父同住卡尔克萨，作为邪恶的眷属忠心侍奉在父亲脚下。但没过多久，他们也像母亲、舅父和外祖母一样开始窃窃私语、争吵算计。他们梦想着权力与继承王位。最终，托图特与塔西洛克不自量力地向父亲发难。哈斯塔始终知晓他们的阴谋，轻而易举地避开了所有陷阱，并以难以描述的恐怖方式毁灭了两个儿子。</p><p>女儿塔西尔达知道兄弟们的阴谋，却拒绝参与，因此得以幸免。但她也没有警告父亲，而是打算先观望阴谋能否成功，再决定自己该站在哪一边。塔西尔达因这无声的背叛受到惩罚。她的父亲，那位不可名状者，将她封在家中，又把整座居所从卡尔克萨撕下，抛入太空。父亲宣称，到了某个不可避免的时刻，她终将获释，并得到自己渴望的一切。</p><p class='basic'>在剧本日志中记录<i>你观看了《卡尔克萨的继承人》演出</i>。每位调查员承受1点精神创伤。控制“卡尔克萨的继承人”弱点的调查员可在其“记忆”旁增加2个计数。</p>",label:{addTwoMemories:"在你的“记忆”旁增加2个计数。",doNotAddMemories:"不增加计数。"}},Ee={title:"寻找碎片",body:"<p>在破衣号上，你和同伴试图找出小行星“碎片”的坐标，以阻止哈斯塔之女塔西尔达升格。分析舰上残余数据后，你与K2-PS187找出三条值得调查的线索；时间紧迫，你们或许应优先前往最有价值的目的地。</p><p class='basic'>调查员必须选择一条此前未选择的线索追查。</p>",trace1:"<p><b>线索1：</b><i>破衣号前往碎片之前的最后一站，是名为厄尔布鲁士的流浪小行星上的研究实验室。该设施研究具有量子行为的材料。你不知道邪教徒意欲何为，但那里的科学家或许能为你指路。</i></p>",trace2:"<p><b>线索2：</b><i>深入分析档案发现，有人入侵了一艘名为怀旧II号的地球勘测船主机，记录还反复提到“隔离”和“不要信任任何人”。若能联络船员，或许能弄清邪教徒的目标。</i></p>",trace3:"<p><b>线索3：</b><i>过去几年，破衣号似乎多次降落在土星的一颗卫星上，航行日志把行动记为“谈判”。K2-PS187指出这很反常，因为太阳系这么远的地方没有已知人类据点。你们可前往这些坐标查明所谓谈判是什么。</i></p>",label:{lostQuantum:"追查线索1。进入冒险IIIa：失落量子。",inTheShadowOfEarth:"追查线索2。进入冒险IIIb：地球阴影。",strangeMoons:"追查线索3。进入冒险IIIc：奇异卫星。"}},Me={title:"幕间II：内省",body:"<p>奇异量子碎片、从米·戈处取得的金盘、来自地球的谜样讯息……你们已奔走太阳系收集拼图碎片，却仍无法拼成全貌。缺少的是能将一切联系起来的关键。而你确定有一处藏着全部答案，只是害怕面对：自己的心灵深处。你能感觉到曾经的邪教徒自我囚在思绪边缘；那个你知道如何找到碎片。进入自己的虚拟心智极其危险，任何小错都可能使你坠入疯狂，但你已准备面对过去。K2-PS187再次调整冷眠舱的梦境协议，让你进入个人记忆；你躺回舱内，开关一拨，意识再次沉落……</p>",searchTheTatterdemalion:"<p class='basic'>调查员可选择花时间搜索破衣号，寻找遗漏的重要细节。若如此做，在“迫近的毁灭”及每位调查员的“记忆”旁各增加1个计数。</p>",sideStory:"<p class='basic'>调查员可通过游玩支线故事进入地球历史模拟，了解这个未来；以划掉“记忆”计数代替支付经验费用。游玩支线获得的经验改为调查员的“记忆”。（若需要，可手动调整剧本日志。）依难度，将下列混乱标记加入混乱袋直到剧本结束：简单（-3）、标准（-5）、困难（-6及邪教徒）、专家（-7及邪教徒）。</p>",introspection1:"<p>过去人生的记忆涌回：向采矿前哨发射导弹、散播模因生物病毒，以及施加于人类的更多难言恶行。曾经的邪教徒必须为暴行负责，而你终于准备好彻底熄灭其在你体内的残影。</p><p class='basic'>每位调查员在下一个冒险开始时额外拥有1资源，并在起始手牌中额外抽1张卡。</p>",label:{searchTheShip:"搜索破衣号。在“迫近的毁灭”和每位调查员的“记忆”旁各增加1个计数。",doNotSearchTheShip:"不搜索飞船。"}},xe={title:"尾声",epilogue1:"<p>逆乎一切可能，人类在第二次末日后幸存。新星光与死者尘埃之间，人类迎来科学与繁荣的黄金时代；当昔日太阳化作的白矮星熄灭，人类已殖民半座星系。部分世界会屈服于古神疯狂，多数仍会生存兴盛。但数十亿年后，宇宙熵仍持续增加，群星逐一黯淡，后继者只能从黑洞的微弱辐射中求生；在漫长得不可计数的时间后，黑洞也会蒸发……</p>",epilogue2:"<p>人类或许与自己的恒星一同消亡了，但宇宙中的生命并非全都归顺古神。真菌状的米·戈科学家带着观察人类所得的无尽知识宝库逃离了太阳系。米·戈的后代延续下来，为满足永无止境的求知欲，在无数星系间探索并建立殖民地。然而亿万年过去，宇宙的总熵依然缓慢而稳定地增长。群星一颗接一颗地暗去，直到那些由昔日米·戈演化而来的生命，只能抽取宇宙中仅存天体，也就是黑洞所释放的微弱辐射来维持生存。即便如此，经过一段有限却无法计数的漫长岁月，就连黑洞也终将蒸发……</p>",epilogue3:"<p>当所有黑洞都消失，只剩彼此遥远的光子与电子构成的真空，宇宙生命也将终结。我们的宇宙迎来冰冷空虚的死亡，留下最大衰变与无尽暗物质的世界——某些人曾称它为卡尔克萨。</p>",epilogue4:"<p>然而人类并不孤单。他们在宇宙中遇到无数外星种族，并分享知识与技术，寻找逆转熵增的方法。最后一块拼图是犹格斯星的米·戈科学家收集的数据：古神首次苏醒前，地球一间幼儿园中六个孩子的大脑信息。最终，在米·戈关键协助下，卡尔克萨王族再次被囚于疯狂的领域，黄色星辰在更光明的重生宇宙中升起。</p>"},St={missionBriefing:_e,heirToCarcosa:Pe,theSearchForFragment:Ee,introspection:Me,epilogue:xe},Ct=Object.freeze(Object.defineProperty({__proto__:null,default:St,epilogue:xe,heirToCarcosa:Pe,introspection:Me,missionBriefing:_e,theSearchForFragment:Ee},Symbol.toStringTag,{value:"Module"})),At=Object.assign({"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/allPointsWest.json":Be,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/base.json":Le,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/harmsWay.json":je,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/interludes.json":ze,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/oneNightOnly.json":qe,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/en/thePrimrosePath.json":Ve,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/zh-cn/base.json":$e,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/zh-cn/interludes.json":Qe,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/zh-cn/oneNightOnly.json":Ze,"/homebrew/circus-ex-mortis/locales/zh-cn/thePrimrosePath.json":tt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/base.json":at,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/electricNightmare.json":nt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/fragmentOfCarcosa.json":rt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/inTheShadowOfEarth.json":lt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/interludes.json":ct,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/lostQuantum.json":pt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/starfall.json":yt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/strangeMoons.json":ft,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/theMachineInYellow.json":wt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/en/theTatterdemalion.json":kt,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/zh-cn/base.json":It,"/homebrew/dark-matter/locales/zh-cn/interludes.json":Ct});function Rt(De="en"){const t={};for(const[We,Ye]of Object.entries(At)){const e=We.match(/\/([^/]+)\/locales\/([^/]+)\/[^/]+\.json$/);if(!e||!e[1]||e[2]!==De)continue;const o=e[1].split("-"),a=(o[0]??"")+o.slice(1).map(i=>i.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+i.slice(1)).join("");t[a]={...t[a]??{},...Ye.default}}return t}export{Rt as h};
